{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle","id":835958,"title":"[Ex3] How to challenge a full solar circle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-23T13:00:48-08:00","id":835958,"title":"[Ex3] How to challenge a full solar circle","content":"I'm finding that it can be very difficult to challenge the might of a full circle of Solar exalts, so I'm making this thread for STs to share their ideas and experiences. Feel free to post non-combat challenges as well, anything to break up the often boring steam-roller sensation of besting obstacle after obstacle without even busting out a full excellency.<br /> <br /> Observations I have made so far:<br /> <br /> 1. Don't let them <i>all</i> get in the first hit; my party has won fight after fight by crashing every enemy in round one, hoarding their initiative, then ending the fight in one round of Decisive attacks. This is an extremely effective tactic, so <i>don't</i> let them use it freely. Ambushes and initiative-modding charms for your antagonists will help.<br /> <br /> 2. Always out-number them; with the new system even just one more combatant on the field makes all the difference. That's one more attack the party can use each round to crash an opponent and prevent them from launching a decisive blow. If you often use battlegroups, I recommend splitting as many &quot;heroic&quot; characters off as needed to keep the numbers <i>at least </i>even. <i>N</i><i>ever</i> write in a final boss fight with only one antagonist.<br /> <br /> 3. The higher the enemy's Soak, the longer the fight; a high soak is just about the only thing besides the Legendary Size ability which I've found can counteract the advantage of wolf pack tactics, even more so than an onslaught negater.<br /> <br /> 4. Beware of initiative hoarding; one of my players regularly builds up to 30+ initiative during combat and never unleashes a Decisive attack because he knows that resetting to base initiative will leave him vulnerable. These players are effectively &quot;tanking&quot; for their party, and the best solution is to avoid them and focus on players who might actually get crashed.<br /> <br /> 5. Assume <i>someone</i> is going to pass every check; in a group of five Solars you'll probably see full coverage for every kind of skill proficiency, so avoid writing in plot elements that assume every member of the party will fail that check. Awareness is a good example: if even one person in your party makes that obscene roll to notice the ninjas approaching from the South, then the ambush you just wrote in isn't going to go off unless you first split the party or prevent them from communicating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 02-23-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:10:14-08:00","id":835973,"title":"","content":"This is a good start. I like number 5 the most. It's a pitfall I've found myself in multiple times in previous editions, and it's no less true in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:46:13-08:00","id":835998,"title":"","content":"Dragon-blooded in numbers, particularly with summoned/browbeaten/allied supernatural support, are brutally effective.<br /> <br /> Fear Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Almost anything without a dice-adder or equivalent effect is going to have a bad time.<br /> <br /> Take advantage of the flexibility offered by opponents possessing sorcery/necromancy and artifacts. Although, obviously, be careful with the latter getting into the hands of your party before you're ready for it.<br /> <br /> Remember, Solars reshape shit and derail plots and that's OK! If they're steamrolling almost everything, well...they're Solars. That's their schtick. If it didn't take an epic effort to seriously stymie them, the setting wouldn't make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T14:24:13-08:00","id":836029,"title":"","content":"Wearing them down works.<br /> <br /> Rather than one big encounter, make it so that there are multiple encounters without giving them much chance at a breather. I often find 2x DB's + Battle group then another 3x DB's + another battle group more dangerous than all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T15:48:41-08:00","id":836068,"title":"","content":"Don't play the game, play the players.<br /> <br /> I know my players as people. Over time, I have gleaned insight into how their personalities influence their play style. When I am designing anything, I first consider their reactions to previous similar encounters. <br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that in a game like Exalted sometimes the best way to handle the might of a party is to deny them the opportunity to use it. Sure, they can probably take a few months and steamroll the local horse tribes, but the Wyld Hunt will have caught up with them. What they really need is to use diplomacy and guile to convince the tribes to unite against the Realm's oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T15:52:22-08:00","id":836075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=836029#post836029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than one big encounter, make it so that there are multiple encounters without giving them much chance at a breather. I often find 2x DB's + Battle group then another 3x DB's + another battle group more dangerous than all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, but I want to caution people that in this edition essence drain is not the death sentence it was in 2nd ed. In combat players always have 5 motes to work with each turn, so they are never completely without magic. Building up a few wound penalties with 2-5 dice Decisive attacks seems to be a more reliable detriment, so even if your most recent antagonist group fails to build up lethal initiative levels it's still worth it to launch a Decisive attack or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T16:46:33-08:00","id":836097,"title":"","content":"I would argue that a Decisive ought to be considered (note: not necessarily selected, but <i>considered</i>) at any Initiative value above 6. It can be tempting to just save up until you can one-shot somebody in a single splattering blow, but at 7 or more you have a reasonably good chance of rolling at least two HLs of damage and knocking an opponent into wound penalties. That tilts things permanently against them. At 10 or higher you have a decent chance of knocking someone straight into their -2's, which is enough to put most folks on the back foot for good. You don't have to kill an enemy to defeat them - if they're worried about actually dying and looking for a way out while nursing a serious injury, they're probably not a threat any longer.<br /> <br /> Obviously there are a lot of tactical items to consider when choosing how to attack, but it really doesn't take a whole lot of Initiative to make a Decisive worth taking. If a good opportunity presents itself (i.e. their current Defense is low and you're not in immediate danger) it's probably worth jumping on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T18:52:56-08:00","id":836144,"title":"","content":"Though I haven't had a chance to test it myself, several people here have also told me that opening combat with an AoE damage spell like Death of Obsidian Butterflies is also a good way to add tension. Potentially you'll put several people into wound penalties right at the outset, and if that blast also wings a few civilians then that adds drama. I'm looking forward to trying it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T19:47:09-08:00","id":836177,"title":"","content":"No one here seems to have noted environmental penalties. A -2 penalty to all rolls because of thick, acrid smoke and 1B/round from the heat of the encroaching forest fire seems like a reasonable way to turn up the stakes in a battle with an ifrit lord<br /> <br /> Falling damage is still exceptionally lethal. Perhaps an earth elemental causes a sudden ravine to appear, or a Nightingale stylist manages to shatter the tower the heroes are standing on with the power of a kiai, or some particularly paranoid lord really truly does have a scorpion pit built underneath the throne room for just this occasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T23:25:12-08:00","id":836269,"title":"","content":"Never underestimate the power of a Battlegroup using its Engage ability. Especially if it is big enough to span a range band or two. Lots of players being grappled simultaneously is harsh, the initiative drain can kill them.<br /> <br /> Doubly (triplely?) if it's commanded by someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T03:43:13-08:00","id":836322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=835998#post835998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-blooded in numbers, particularly with summoned/browbeaten/allied supernatural support, are brutally effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big issue there is potentially further devaluing of DBs. When every fight requires 1-2 DBs per Solar PC you've now got a scaling problem where anything less is trivial and anything more risks TPK. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=835998#post835998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, Solars reshape shit and derail plots and that's OK! If they're steamrolling almost everything, well...they're Solars. That's their schtick. If it didn't take an epic effort to seriously stymie them, the setting wouldn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>this is a narrative setting conceit that makes for nothing short of an exhausting gameplay premise, especially if it's present from the first instant post-chargen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:08:13-08:00","id":836353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=836322#post836322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big issue there is potentially further devaluing of DBs. When every fight requires 1-2 DBs per Solar PC you've now got a scaling problem where anything less is trivial and anything more risks TPK.<br /> <br /> <br /> this is a narrative setting conceit that makes for nothing short of an exhausting gameplay premise, especially if it's present from the first instant post-chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it's probably not a popular opinion, but I'm more in the camp that Solars should be totally awesome, and use other things to rise to absolutely ridiculous challenges. Players are smart, and if STs want them to do it, they can find a way. I might even have killed more gods in DnD than in exalted, and relatively speaking most of the gods in exalted suck*.<br /> <br /> And I know there's lots of ways around it, but as Zel said, it can be kind of exhausting at times. And it can leave the players feel cheated when every third session has a challenge specifically targeted to circumvent their specialties. And with a full circle that's a pretty damn limited set of things. It's DEFINITELY not as bad as second edition though, but still having some troubles. It might also be that I don't know the system that well as well, we'll see.<br /> <br /> *Like as in fighting a salt god vs fighting Tiamat is on a totally different scale. Not the concept of gods in exalted being bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:22:48-08:00","id":836360,"title":"","content":"TBH just sometimes going &quot;ok fuck it, you're strong beefy Solars, you can handle it&quot; and dropping a Nemissary or Octavian in there, backed up by a couple war ghosts/blood apes and shit gets real. I think I'm personally beginning to grasp what's dangerous, and can adjust accordingly. Just write up a powerful spirit if your Solars thump everything.<br /> <br /> The best advice in this thread so far, IMHO, was the &quot;play the player&quot;-line. Look at your players tactics and usual approaches, and counter them. If your most deadly guy is a Single Point stylist, swarm him, if he's a White Reaper stylist, don't swarm him. If he's a melee tank, whittle him down from distance, etc.; of course it's never that simple, but if you players specialize, have the antagonists counter-specialize. But don't overdo it or you get a min/maxing arms race. If your players specialize hard in something, they have to feel their character being great at it, or they'll be driven to up their numbers even more, that's unhealthy imho.<br /> <br /> Luckily in my group nobody's a combat supernal (3 characters, no Dawn, heh.) making balance easier.<br /> But still, if your Solars curbstomp everything I have to ask:<br /> Did you throw a Fakharu-sized opponent at them? <br /> Because that motherfucker would smoke <i>my</i> party.<br /> <br /> Edit: I just realized you weren't asking combat-only, which is funny, because in my games, there tends to be very little combat, yet I only thought about, well, combat. I shall post some non-combat stuff later, am out of time for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:40:39-08:00","id":836372,"title":"","content":"A quick way to boost BGs ability to fight without having to add another moving piece into the system is to give them what I call a free-commander. Each BG has a commander you give a command dice pool to. His role will only be to lead the unit, he can be target by the players ofc. Just use the magnitude track for BG for health levels (represented as bodyguards or him just being a bit tough to take down) So if you take him down that might cause a rout check or not, up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Easily ups the danger from facing battlegroups, withouth adding yet another initiative number to track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:21:33-08:00","id":836544,"title":"","content":"Something else to keep in mind is the kind of game you want to run. If you're like me, and you DO expect Solars to start changing the world (or just their little corner of it) from almost session 1, then you probably want a fair number of conflicts (combat and otherwise) to be dramatic, but ultimately diversions to the story of the characters' success in making change (just because Solars DO effect change doesn't mean they get the changes they want). You can feel free to use other Celestials, DBs, and Celestial gods as necessary for large threats.<br /> <br /> If you lean more to the Zel persuasion, then you need to spend more time investing in tactics and strategies to make it feel gritty for the players. Another way to do that is to be more strict with training time and XP. It's much easier to challenge a Dawn with three named mortal swordmasters BEFORE the Dawn has a hundred XP.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T23:58:20-08:00","id":836885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=835998#post835998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, Solars reshape shit and derail plots and that's OK! If they're steamrolling almost everything, well...they're Solars. That's their schtick. If it didn't take an epic effort to seriously stymie them, the setting wouldn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is certainly true that the Solar exalted are &quot;big damn heroes&quot; of the highest degree, my zenith caste has yet to take damage five sessions in and he makes a point of being at the front of every combat. Ideally I'd like my players to feel a sense of accomplishment, which requires that they both affect major change AND feel as if their victories were hard-won. The latter can be challenging in third edition's narrative combat system.<br /> <br /> Has anyone had a chance to test abilities/charms that allow for reflexive decisive attacks? I have noticed several in the animal write-ups that conditionally allow you to follow up a successful withering attack with a decisive blow, and it seems like that might be a great way to shift the flow of combat in the enemy's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:53:20-08:00","id":838511,"title":"","content":"Here's a non-combat tip: if you plan to make mysteries a primary element of your adventure, don't reduce solving them down to one Intelligence + Investigation roll with an obscene difficulty. Instead, break one investigation down into many smaller rolls to find clues and let your players draw their own conclusions.<br /> <br /> Example: instead of one roll to determine who killed the local seneschal, players might roll to establish whether the attacker used magic, what the murder weapon was, if they had help, or if the attack took place elsewhere. Encourage out of character guessing backed up by rolls and storytelling until the player can put the clues together themselves for a more satisfying win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 02-28-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T07:45:46-08:00","id":838635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838511#post838511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a non-combat tip: if you plan to make mysteries a primary element of your adventure, don't reduce solving them down to one Intelligence + Investigation roll with an obscene difficulty. Instead, break one investigation down into many smaller rolls.<br /> <br /> Example: instead of one roll to determine who killed the local seneschal, players might roll to establish whether the attacker used magic, what the murder weapon was, if they had help, or if the attack took place elsewhere. Encourage out of character guessing backed up by rolls and storytelling until the player can put the clues together themselves for a more satisfying win.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This does tend to break down if you have someone with a heavy Investigation investment, but doesn't completely obviate this as a method. The investigation tree just tends to shoot out plot hooks in a different kind of way, as there are some great, holistic case scene charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:29:08-08:00","id":838657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=836360#post836360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH just sometimes going &quot;ok fuck it, you're strong beefy Solars, you can handle it&quot; and dropping a Nemissary or Octavian in there, backed up by a couple war ghosts/blood apes and shit gets real. I think I'm personally beginning to grasp what's dangerous, and can adjust accordingly. Just write up a powerful spirit if your Solars thump everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can quickly turn into &quot;welp, second Tuesday of the month, time to fight Octavian again.&quot; At least until someone up and kills him with GET, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=836544#post836544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you lean more to the Zel persuasion, then you need to spend more time investing in tactics and strategies to make it feel gritty for the players. Another way to do that is to be more strict with training time and XP. It's much easier to challenge a Dawn with three named mortal swordmasters BEFORE the Dawn has a hundred XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not gritty so much as...it shouldn't be super casually easy, because that just gets boring to run, and, after a ton of successes without any meaningful challenge in the process, boring to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:55:17-08:00","id":838664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838657#post838657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not gritty so much as...it shouldn't be super casually easy, because that just gets boring to run, and, after a ton of successes without any meaningful challenge in the process, boring to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that's starting to trip up the One Ring campaign I'm currently in.<br /> <br /> In One Ring, as your characters accrue XP, they start hitting enemies a lot more often and a lot harder, and more potent enemies can hit them a lot easier and a lot harder in turn... but while enemies can be made harder to kill, player characters cannot. There's a hard cap on how much health you can have and how difficult you are to hit, and most players will hit that hard cap very, very early.<br /> <br /> Our GM has had a goddamn nightmare of a time balancing encounters for us as we become more and badass, because he would prefer not to murder us, but would also like us to be having fights that aren't just an hour and a half of &quot;rolling dice until all the orcs, which will never hit you, die.&quot; But if the orcs <i>do</i> start hitting us, <i>we'll</i> die. Very, very fast, in fact.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:36:07-08:00","id":838679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838664#post838664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that's starting to trip up the One Ring campaign I'm currently in.<br /> <br /> In One Ring, as your characters accrue XP, they start hitting enemies a lot more often and a lot harder, and more potent enemies can hit them a lot easier and a lot harder in turn... but while enemies can be made harder to kill, player characters cannot. There's a hard cap on how much health you can have and how difficult you are to hit, and most players will hit that hard cap very, very early.<br /> <br /> Our GM has had a goddamn nightmare of a time balancing encounters for us as we become more and badass, because he would prefer not to murder us, but would also like us to be having fights that aren't just an hour and a half of &quot;rolling dice until all the orcs, which will never hit you, die.&quot; But if the orcs <i>do</i> start hitting us, <i>we'll</i> die. Very, very fast, in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same issue with Shadowrun really, except soak is cheap and stacking it isn't so hard. But you do reach that point where you just can't add health boxes. Also I would say the same issue with FFG Star Wars, where it's really hard to actually kill a PC, but easy to put them in crits early in a mission, which take a while to kill and cumulatively stack on making it easier to actually kill them. Or in L5R, where offense scaling is just a matter of adding additional unkept dice, but defense is a derived formula, health scales very slowly (based on a Ring, meaning you need to raise both Traits that are part of the Ring, and Trait costs scale exponentially), and soak is <i>wholly</i> inadequate unless you're in a super specific build. It's a fundamental problem for systems where offense outstrips defense (as it often does). But the flipside, where your PCs can easily dominate opponents with no risk, is like playing a very slow video game, and about as satisfying.<br /> <br /> This is kinda disappointing to hear about One Ring. A friend of mine wanted to run it but I feel like I should pass this on to him, so he can better evaluate whether he wants to get into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-28-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:16:29-08:00","id":838725,"title":"","content":"The invincible or dead binary issue also crops up on Aberrant with alarming frequency, and it's not limited to straight up combat. If a given PC hasn't justified and purchased all the various shield powers, a psychic/strobe character can easily overwhelm just about anyone. And even if they do, Mega-Socials and Enhancements don't have much in the way of default counters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:01:09-08:00","id":838908,"title":"","content":"Out of interest, do you guys have a lot of combats that are supposed to be serious?<br /> <br /> I've done over 20 sessions, and so far they've had one serious combat against two Exalts, one combat against a mortal sorcerer and some raiders where the PCs took a bit of damage when he ambushed them, then kicked ass, a combat against some martial artists where the worst combat guy got crashed and that was it, and 2 or 3 combats against demons that were piss-easy. I mean, most of these combats are there for fluff reasons (ie a demon isn't going to let you waltz in without a fight, even though he's horribly outmatched, because he's bound), not because I'm actually trying to make it hard for the essence 4 PCs. There's only one fight so far where I was actually trying to challenge them a bit, and it wasn't supposed to be extremely difficult.<br /> <br /> Next session, I'll have a combat which I think might be tricky for them, against a whole bunch of DBs, and they're split up, and I could maybe possibly see the Lunar with only excellencies dying, though I don't see it as very likely. But that's after about 20 sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:19:31-08:00","id":838974,"title":"","content":"I generally, in 2e, just went around the rules. Needed Fey to be bad ass? Have a fey noble swordsman with Jade artifact sword, and an Illusion/real/camouflage/smoke/dancing cloak that -10 dice for all the above stuff coming into to play as defense. They would have to activate perfect sight, look through illusions, ignore cover, and ignore defend other. I also had most Fey warriors in Behemoth guises, shaped liked D and D dragons, with the foot soldier goblins exactly like the Draconians from Dragonlance.<br /> <br /> Want stuff to be climactic? Build your NPC like PCs, with escape routes and underhanded traps, like burning sandstorms that earth/fire DBs and elementals are immune to, but do 2B or 2L, plus an environmental penalty. Or have Bowman 500 bowman, in 5 battle groups of a hundred, on horses ride around the PCs, at long Range( Parthians used this to good effect against roman legions under Crasus at the Battle of Carhae). Or have have Firwands with bayonets set up in 2 BC, where one will step back, while another step forward, so they can regroups( ie make a Morale roll to heal/recover). Or even 5 BCs of 5 Super elite Mortals each with excellent weapons or access to MA charms( Enlightened 2e Mortals or Godblooded).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:48:36-08:00","id":838985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838908#post838908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of interest, do you guys have a lot of combats that are supposed to be serious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I'd be alright with one fight per session being an actual challenge, but I started off with a mortal tier prelude where I outright <i>promised</i> my players that I would kill several of their characters (they made 4-5 each) and I failed to kill any of them. Since then, I've been trying to challenge them on principle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally, in 2e, just went around the rules. Needed Fey to be bad ass? Have a fey noble swordsman with Jade artifact sword, and an Illusion/real/camouflage/smoke/dancing cloak that -10 dice for all the above stuff coming into to play as defense. They would have to activate perfect sight, look through illusions, ignore cover, and ignore defend other. I also had most Fey warriors in Behemoth guises, shaped liked D and D dragons, with the foot soldier goblins exactly like the Draconians from Dragonlance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable. Heavy internal penalties are nice way to level a playing field that doesn't necessarily have to have a saving throw to resist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Want stuff to be climactic? Build your NPC like PCs, with escape routes and underhanded traps, like burning sandstorms that earth/fire DBs and elementals are immune to, but do 2B or 2L, plus an environmental penalty. Or have Bowman 500 bowman, in 5 battle groups of a hundred, on horses ride around the PCs, at long Range( Parthians used this to good effect against roman legions under Crasus at the Battle of Carhae). Or have have Firwands with bayonets set up in 2 BC, where one will step back, while another step forward, so they can regroups( ie make a Morale roll to heal/recover). Or even 5 BCs of 5 Super elite Mortals each with excellent weapons or access to MA charms( Enlightened 2e Mortals or Godblooded).</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u200b</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> I'm actually finding that environmental hazards are laughably easy to ignore in this edition, as even the most punishing have a difficulty of only five to ignore <i>completely </i>at each interval. So far none of my players have had a problem evading these, even the ones without a focus in the associated skill. <br /> <br /> As for battlegroups, the ones without commanders die only slightly slower than individual characters with the same stats, get ganged up on by the entire party and end up becoming giant sacks of initiative for my players to steal before using on individual actors of actual note. A commander can make them threatening by adding their successes on an Order action as bonus dice on their attack rolls, but don't count on the battlegroup holding up by itself. The party will rely on withering attacks only (because decisive attacks aren't worth using on a BG), and build a comfortable buffer of initiative that makes the fight one-sided because while the party can swing back quickly from low initiative the BG cannot.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:57:16-08:00","id":838987,"title":"","content":"They only get 1 initiative per attack on a battle group though, and the battle groups can sometimes do a fair bit to them, so I don't find they're anywhere near as good for the players to harvest initiative from as a weak npc who isn't in a battle group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T23:22:33-08:00","id":838994,"title":"","content":"Have PCs go against a Elite Fighters, with Elite drill, Size 5, Might 1 heavy Cavalry in heavy armor, with slashings swords, Bows, shields, and lances, horses with heavy barding, with a special charge attacks that adds extra damage and counts as an area attack that's harder to parry/dogde. Have the Cavalry start out at long range with bows, them switch to lances. Remember that an initiative crashed PC gets health levels in damage instead of initiative damage. The Might 1 comes from blessing similar to brides of ahlat,<br /> In my game, to make Shields more useful, I made it so that you could do a charge attack and use them at full defensive, with the flurry penalty. Or have special abilities as BC gambit( Shield wall +1-3 defense, wall of Lances- can defende or be attacked first, the Charge of Heavy Cavalry+4 withering attack from lances and trample).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T00:15:16-08:00","id":839005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838985#post838985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually finding that environmental hazards are laughably easy to ignore in this edition, as even the most punishing have a difficulty of only five to ignore <i>completely </i>at each interval. So far none of my players have had a problem evading these, even the ones without a focus in the associated skill.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838985#post838985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for battlegroups, the ones without commanders die only slightly slower than individual characters with the same stats, get ganged up on by the entire party and end up becoming giant sacks of initiative for my players to steal before using on individual actors of actual note.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Like The Wizard of Oz says, BGs don't get init bonuses.<br /> <br /> At some point you need to write up these encounters turn by turn for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T00:19:30-08:00","id":839006,"title":"","content":"Well my players hit essence 2 a little while ago, maybe almost halfway to three now? So I threw a tyrant lizard and Octavian at them at the same time. It was a good fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:15:16-08:00","id":839017,"title":"","content":"How'd they do?<br /> <br /> To be honest, I tend to just try to run whatever fight I think is reasonable fluff-wise, rather than what I think will challenge the PCs in the fight.<br /> <br /> So, for example, I statted up a really badass elite Wyld Hunt, which turned up after 20 sessions of them just fighting non-Exalts (because Exalts aren't that common, and it took time for the Wyld Hunt to hear enough about where/who they are).<br /> The Wyld Hunt was hiding in a hidden cellar under a shrine, ready to ambush them at a feast. I wasn't sure if the PCs would discover the ambush or not: as it was, they did, because they realised their Dragonblood allies were up to something (that being that they'd betrayed them to the Wyld Hunt), thanks to good Read Intentions rolls, and then found them with the Lunar's Perception charms, and so they unleashed the Magma Kraken, which of course is pretty devastating against five people in a basement not expecting a Magma Kraken.<br /> Next session, they may well fight half a Wyld Hunt, who are pretty injured. Probably not a very challenging fight, but that's the reward for discovering the ambush.<br /> <br /> I think the thing is, my players tend to either not enjoy combats as much as I, or enjoy them for half an hour or so, and then get bored (as do I: actually, I try to design foes that will hit hard but not last that long, so the fight doesn't drag on too badly). So, I don't really run a very heavy combat game. Mostly the combats are there because I feel they ought to be there, for story reasons.<br /> <br /> If the players loved combat, I'd probably do a lot more and go out of my way to challenge the players.<br /> <br /> Also, I guess if they were Essence 1. They recently hit Essence 5, so it seems infeasible that they'd run into something very challenging every 2-3 sessions. But a lot more things are challenging for Essence 1 characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-29-2016, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T05:56:50-08:00","id":839091,"title":"","content":"So I'm the Dawn in DrLoveMonkey's game. We did fairly well, the fight wasn't a cakewalk by any means. Though the Tyrant Lizard was totally in there so the Deadly Predator Method(? The capstone survival charm if that's not it) Ox-Dragon could be used at some point in the game. Lots of motes were spent by most of the party, with myself and at least one other running off of just the 5 mote/turn drip by the end. I probably had the best setup for fighting him with Fire and Stones Strike and Iron Whirlwind/Invincible Fury of the Dawn. Having Octavian's mount there as a separate combatant definitely helped with killing him, but it also split up the party's attacks so I'm not sure if it would have gone better with everyone wailing on him or not.<br /> <br /> So we had a perfect circle (Dawn Melee Supernal, Zenith Survival Supernal, Twilight Craft Supernal w/ Sorcery, Night Stealth Supernal with Thrown, and Eclipse Occult Supernal with Archery), as well as a Dusk (NPC) that was the Zenith's wife and a Wood Aspect (NPC) that was with the Night. I fought Octavian, the Zenith Deadly Predator Methoded both his Dog and Ox-Dragon and sent the dog to fight Octavian and the Ox-Dragon to fight the Tyrant Lizard while he turned on Battle Anthem of the Solar Exalted. The Twilight summoned the terrestrial cloud spell and used that to take him and the eclipse up into the air while he charged up a flight of the brilliant raptor. The Night, Eclipse and Dragonblood were taking whatever opportunity shots they could against Octavian or his Agate. The Dusk was off fighting another NPC Abyssal off-screen.<br /> <br /> Myself and Octavian were reasonably matched in that our withering attacks didn't end up doing a whole heck of a lot to each other (Him having high soak, and me boosting my parry so he didn't hit me). It was once I had made my Invincible Fury of the Dawn attacks that dealt some decisive damage and applied some silly onslaught penalties to him that helped allow the Wood Aspect to get in a REAL good withering shot on him and allowed some more attacks to get through to stack on some more damage. The Ox-Dragon basically went off and fought the Tyrant Lizard, I didn't end up paying a huge amount of attention to the other combatants because I was trying to sort out what my next turn would be usually. I ended up having to attack the Agate twice using Peony Blossom to build up a bunch of initiative to then next turn Iron Whirlwind Octavian for lethal.<br /> <br /> There wasn't a huge amount of health level damage (though the Eclipse almost got one-shotted by his scream), but there was a LOT of back and forth in the fight which I think is just as important. There was a time where I honestly wasn't sure HOW we were going to beat Octavian, the high soak, high hardness, and ability to gain initiative from decisive damage that he's taken AND the ability to stem HL damage to his current wound penalty made him REAL nasty to fight. Having Battle Anthem up really helped our side as you always gained SOME initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8837-supermadol","name":"SuperMadol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:21:03-08:00","id":839147,"title":"","content":"He must be extremely tough to fight that many Exalts at once!<br /> <br /> DrLoveMonkey, how did you find the fight to run?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:40:12-08:00","id":839161,"title":"","content":"He had like 17 Soak and 10 Hardness, so you weren't easily taking him down in initiative (For point of reference, before Fire and Stones Strike and overflow successes, his soak took away my entire damage pool, forcing me to use my min damage of my daiklave), and because he had a decent hardness it also meant that people couldn't just throw what initiative they had at him trying to inflict SOME damage. He also never got crashed, which would have changed things a fair bit. There was just no good way to knock him down in initiative without just straight up dogpiling him and hoping min damage chipped away enough. And then he'd either hit you back with a withering attack and gain initiative, or gain a bunch when he was dealt HL damage. It was not a quick fight by any means, he's a resilient opponent, but there are some holes in his defenses. Onslaught penalties in particular get to him.<br /> <br /> Him and the Nephwrack I think are fairly well made adversaries in that they have ways to stay relevant to the fight (being difficult to damage and gaining initiative from not normal means, and difficulty to attack as well as attack redirection, forcing the players to spend extra on raising a defense against the attack redirection as well as on their normal attack/defense respectively.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8837-supermadol","name":"SuperMadol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:27:08-08:00","id":839194,"title":"","content":"It does seem to me that, while soak is pretty good, it's really important for a boss fight. In fact, often the boss wants to be fighting by himself and not having lieutenants that assistants could get initiative from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:33:01-08:00","id":839200,"title":"","content":"The big thing with High soak bosses is that if you don't give the players SOME way of generating initiative it'll start getting frustrating for them. &quot;I hit, roll min damage, oh look 2 successes. and the boss hit me back for like 6-7, and I'm lower then he started&quot;. Also having other combatants helps reduce the dog pile and onslaught penalties on the boss. I think the idea is more to have the big boss AND a competent underling there, someone that's scary enough that the party feels they should devote some manpower to tackling both targets without one being a pushover or mook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8837-supermadol","name":"SuperMadol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:32:11-08:00","id":839251,"title":"","content":"There was also his Agata and an essence three day caste, but the day caste went and took the dusk caste into personal combat. Also the party had an allied dawn and liminal who thankfully couldn't show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:57:26-08:00","id":839267,"title":"","content":"Just finished my short Mystery Campaign with three Solars (Dawn, Night, and Eclipse).<br /> <br /> 1. I had to do some handwaving so the Keen Scent players could just add the killer's smell to the library and go around time sniffing everyone for the murderer.<br /> <br /> 2. The Dragonblooded QC were a joke to the Dawn. He didn't really even pick up that many offensive charms and he one shotted the Air Aspect QC in round two. (Of course this could be because I wasn't playing the character efficiently. The Air Aspect was more worried about retaliation from his fellow monk he just failed to murder and didn't see this &quot;mortal&quot; as a threat. )<br /> <br /> It was agreed that we will have to wait until the Dragonblooded book came out for us to play Ex3. I want to run a Political Realm Civil War game and the Dragonblooded QC aren't really enough to challenge a Solar. I'm not mechanic savvy enough to rebuild the Dragonblooded Charm set in Ex3 either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:12:48-08:00","id":839279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=839267#post839267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished my short Mystery Campaign with three Solars (Dawn, Night, and Eclipse).<br /> <br /> 1. I had to do some handwaving so the Keen Scent players could just add the killer's smell to the library and go around time sniffing everyone for the murderer.<br /> <br /> 2. The Dragonblooded QC were a joke to the Dawn. He didn't really even pick up that many offensive charms and he one shotted the Air Aspect QC in round two. (Of course this could be because I wasn't playing the character efficiently. The Air Aspect was more worried about retaliation from his fellow monk he just failed to murder and didn't see this &amp;quot;mortal&amp;quot; as a threat. )<br /> <br /> It was agreed that we will have to wait until the Dragonblooded book came out for us to play Ex3. I want to run a Political Realm Civil War game and the Dragonblooded QC aren't really enough to challenge a Solar. I'm not mechanic savvy enough to rebuild the Dragonblooded Charm set in Ex3 either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm starting up a DB NPC for the next game and she's essence five with shining ice mirror. She's going to try and duel the dawn before he gets to essence 2 and I'm hoping she doesn't just die in the second round of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:57:47-08:00","id":839659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=838987#post838987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They only get 1 initiative per attack on a battle group though, and the battle groups can sometimes do a fair bit to them, so I don't find they're anywhere near as good for the players to harvest initiative from as a weak npc who isn't in a battle group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just reread that rule and I can't believe I missed this. I'm glad you corrected me! I wonder what the rationale is for that rule though? Seems like beating up a bunch of mooks would be a good way to build combat steam, frankly. In answer to your later reply, I personally love action scenes and cannot get enough of them. I love that Exalted mechanically encourages stunting from players, and I like building up the fight scenes before and after the session. So that's just a personal preference thing in my case.<br /> <br /> Thank you SuperMadol for the play-by-play. I see someone else noticed what I did about high Soak antagonists, so that's comforting. Also an interesting point about &quot;gaining initiative in unconventional ways&quot; I might have to play with that a bit for my next combat.<br /> <br /> My next story will likely involve a party of Terrestrial exalt antagonists, but I haven't used them in Ex3 yet. Does anyone have pointers for me? Charms they felt worked well or ones they suggest ignoring or buffing for my game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T06:55:25-08:00","id":839864,"title":"","content":"No problem KindledRadial, it was an end of campaign fight that was supposed to be difficult but enjoyable, and I think it faired quite well at that. As for the battlegroup thing I think it's less that beating up the mooks builds up combat steam and more like you're spending what combat steam you build up on fighting them, netting out to no real gains except when knocking off a magnitude track I think it was? Making them go down a size? Something like that.<br /> <br /> The thing in particular with gaining initiative in unconventional ways is that if you're outnumbered you just aren't going to win that initiative fight. if it's a 2 v 1 that one guy needs to deal with both onslaught penalties making him easier to hit AND two attacks sapping away his initiative. For each round he has to somehow put out twice the amount of withering damage then one opponent just to stay initiative neutral! But if he can passively sap some initiative from those two guys a turn, or generate some himself it becomes much easier to keep up with things.<br /> <br /> I have a very informal stream of thought kinda thing floating around on a google doc about what sort of pitfalls an antagonist can run into combat wise and thoughts on how to deal with them. I should read through the antagonist section and flesh that out sometime to post here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8837-supermadol","name":"SuperMadol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T08:51:04-08:00","id":839941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=839659#post839659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread that rule and I can't believe I missed this. I'm glad you corrected me! I wonder what the rationale is for that rule though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so that battle groups are effective counterweights to your PCs rather than giant Initiative pi\u00f1atas. Your experience with PCs casually curbstomping every fight so far seems like a pretty definitive illustration of why that is so important, as I suspect a big part of it has to do with this misread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:20:43-08:00","id":840045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperMadol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=839864#post839864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a very informal stream of thought kinda thing floating around on a google doc about what sort of pitfalls an antagonist can run into combat wise and thoughts on how to deal with them. I should read through the antagonist section and flesh that out sometime to post here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:03:48-08:00","id":840077,"title":"","content":"Well.....someone is looking forward to my ramblings! That was unexpected, guess I'll have to follow through and get something written up in the next few days. (No pressure right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8837-supermadol","name":"SuperMadol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:10:45-08:00","id":840129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperMadol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=839864#post839864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have a very informal stream of thought kinda thing floating around on a google doc about what sort of pitfalls an antagonist can run into combat wise and thoughts on how to deal with them. I should read through the antagonist section and flesh that out sometime to post here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also very much like to read these observations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T22:32:37-08:00","id":842414,"title":"","content":"Here's a general piece of storytelling advice: &quot;one large fire is much easier to deal with than several small ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you only have one bad guy, doing one bad thing, in one location, at one time, then the entire party will dog pile that one guy and in short order overcome him. Now if it's one bad guy and several henchmen they'll have to juggle targets in that combat. If those henchmen are across town pillaging the local citizenry then you might prompt a party split to deal with that and now your one big bad is dealing with much better odds while his flunkies take the fall.<br /> <br /> Also a good idea in general: if you make an area/character/thing important, always have <i>something</i> planned for it. I almost lost two players last game because they stuck with the mortals while the rest of the party flew off to fight the big bad, so try and cover your bases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:50:26-08:00","id":843002,"title":"","content":"I just ran a fight with two good battle groups and 2 high-stat DBs, one of whom was using Single Point, against essentially the Eclipse and the Changing Moon, and a large but rubbish battle group (the other PCs were 5 range bands away). The enemies also rolled really well. One battle group got 14 successes to hit, with +19 damage, and Ringing Anvil Onslaught (so they got to make a second attack), in the first turn, on both PCs and the battle group.<br /> <br /> During the whole fight, the Changing Moon took 2 bashing. And healed one of those. The Eclipse took no damage. Right at the end, when they turned up, the Zenith and Twilight took 1 lethal each.<br /> <br /> Challenging 300xp Celestials without throwing 2nd circles at them or other Celestials (which they have not much reason to be facing) is really, really hard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was pleased however, that the fight only took 2 hours. Which considering that it was the most complex fight I've run in 3rd (and probably more complex than a lot of 2nd ed fights I ran), I think was good. Fights seem to take less time in 3rd ed. They're still long, but not so much. It's probably the lack of flurries.<br /> Took me like 2 hours to prepare though, checking all the stats and charms.<br /> Hopefully I can re-use some of the stuff though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:18:54-08:00","id":844942,"title":"","content":"I felt I should update this with the results of my most recent game.<br /> <br /> So we did a big Caste swap this last week and now the player most adept at playing the game to win is playing the Dawn and he built a defend other melee tank beast. I always get great RP from this player, but he dominates game systems and is about twice as hard to challenge as anyone else at the table. This became very evident during their one combat encounter involving a Size 2 Might 1 battlegroup of Great Cats, four Great Cat single combatants and an E5 war god I spliced together: anyone in range of the Dawn's <i>War Lion Stance</i> took no damage that combat, and everyone outside of that died or was grappled into submission during turn one.<br /> <br /> Observations:<br /> 1) Rolling multiple ambushes for multiple actors is more challenging, but probably not worth the effort. I was concerned that if I rolled one Stealth check for all the enemies that someone in the party would overcome the results and the Great Cats would lose their biggest combat advantage, so I had each actor roll Stealth or Awareness and compared the results to determine who could ambush who. This worked great in a challenge sense, since the battlegroup got an obscene result on their Ambush strategy roll and ambushed everyone in the party, but then there was all this nonsense about how Great Cat A could take an ambush round if it attacked player D but not C or B, and it was just a mess. Probably wasted a full half hour just on that surprise round.<br /> <br /> 2) Defend other should always apply to one ward against one attack, not to several wards against one area attack. I allowed this because the imagery was cool and kicked myself in the butt the rest of the fight. If I could do this over again I'd allow my Dawn to defend other as many people as he wanted using <i>War Lion Stance</i> but only if he activated it for every <i>character</i> he defended, not every <i>attack. </i>If I had done this I would have mote-tapped him in two or three turns.<br /> <br /> 3) Powers and abilities that allow you to follow a withering attack with a decisive attack in the same turn, especially with extra decisive damage dice adders, are <i>very </i>effective. The Great Cat that killed a party member (I allowed them to get a revival by the medic afterwards) used <i>Leaping Pounce</i> and <i>Mauling Bite </i>to slay the second most combat capable character in round one, <i>without</i> the benefits of Stealth. It wasn't even an exceptionally great damage roll.<br /> <br /> 4) Keep track of how many friendlies you have on the player's side. We have five actual players but two animal familiars, one human and one terrestrial retainer and one bound demon in the fray as well and honestly I don't think the power variance is that steep in this new system. If you have five players and five lesser minions, then really that's ten characters you gotta prepare for in combat.<br /> <br /> Today's helpful hint is: If you have a scene where all the party should be challenged by something that only one of them specializes in, write one challenge that will keep the novices entertained and a harder, separate challenge for your specialist to sink their teeth into. Otherwise your novices will feel outclassed or your specialist will feel like they wasted their charm investment.<br /> <br /> Examples might include writing a super strong &quot;boss&quot; for your Dawn to fight while your party keeps the minions off him, letting the party do research legwork while your Twilight puts the final pieces of a mystery together, sending the party out to deliver bribes while your Eclipse continues treating with a regional power, setting the party with a series of fantastical feats while the Zenith exalts their accomplishments to the town, or have everyone else cause a distraction while your Night sneaks into a fortified position. These are also great ways to justify the Caste-related Solar XP for everyone at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:15:21-08:00","id":845118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=844942#post844942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">rest of the fight. If I could do this over again I'd allow my Dawn to defend other as many people as he wanted using <i>War Lion Stance</i> but only if he activated it for every <i>character</i> he defended, not every <i>attack. </i>If I had done this I would have mote-tapped him in two or three turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>War Lion Stance explicitly says that it applies to exactly one ward, for the entire scene, and that defending anyone else requires dropping commitment to this Charm. It is Reflexive, so he <i>could </i>target swap at-will, but doing so would require him to drop and re-activate the Charm every time he wants to do so at 2m a pop. That would get expensive really fast. It also has the range limitation so anybody not at Close range is an invalid target, and it automatically ends if the current target is ever out of range. It sounds like you let the player get away with way, way too much here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:20:21-08:00","id":845151,"title":"","content":"Yeah, also the ability to use a shield to flurry a total defense action, that said without the latter shields are pretty underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:19:21-08:00","id":845234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=845151#post845151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, also the ability to use a shield to flurry a total defense action, that said without the latter shields are pretty underwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity, I let him flurry a full defense and defend other action. Full defense cannot normally be flurried with anything, and shields remove this limitation for everything except attack actions.<br /> <br /> I stand by this one. Without this there is literally no reason to take a small or large shield that I can even imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:26:48-08:00","id":845366,"title":"","content":"Arguably if a single enemy fails stealth then none of them are going to get an ambush - their target is now on high alert that someone is being sneaky. This is why stealth forces tend to be small groups, not large ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:54:42-08:00","id":845501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Today's helpful hint is: If you have a scene where all the party should be challenged by something that only one of them specializes in, write one challenge that will keep the novices entertained and a harder, separate challenge for your specialist to sink their teeth into. Otherwise your novices will feel outclassed or your specialist will feel like they wasted their charm investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very important thing in Exalted fights, where, unlike DnD, some people are just literally much better at combat. A boss and his lieutenants, or a boss and a battle group. When one of my players had a Dawn with DV 13, and the rest were at most decent at combat, I realised this was the way to go.<br /> <br /> I have also found that the number of minions the PCs bring can be overwhelming. Both to fight, and to run. I mean, the player can run them themselves to some extent, but it's still a thing.<br /> In the last fight I ran, there were only 2 PCs in the combat, but one of them brought a dragon, a Jokun and a Vaktri with them.<br /> And his battle group of Greenmaws would have joined them were it not for the fact he'd left them watching the rear in case the Wyld Hunt ambushed them.<br /> There was also a ghost that the party's necromancer had sent to join the combat too.<br /> <br /> I actually once got all the players to each play one of the sorcerer's bound spirits, but they weren't at all familiar with their charms, so it didn't work, and they weren't interested in it really.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will say that 3rd ed is better about this than 2nd ed though.<br /> Firstly, when a sorcerer has 6 blood apes, that's one battle group, for whom you can roll one attack against most or all of the enemies, rather than rolling 18 attacks.<br /> Secondly, spirits don't have a ton of charms that no-one's really familiar with which take ages to find in the back of the book. They're much easier to run for both players and ST.<br /> Third, it normally takes your action to make your mount attack, or use one of the attack-enhancing survival charms for your familiar, or to make a roll to enhance your battle groups attacks.<br /> Fourth, demons aren't making a ton of attacks with Principle of Motion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:10:46-07:00","id":846735,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, how did they get to DV 13? Was it sustainable? Did they use Parry or Evasion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:57:55-07:00","id":846867,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to remember. Hmmm... Dex 5, Essence 3, Dodge 5 (+1 specialty), Hearthstone bracers, that's 9 already. Thunderbolt shield was I think another 3. Then I think they had another artefact for 1 more, but I don't remember exactly.<br /> <br /> This was in 2nd ed of course, in 3rd ed you can't get such big defences sustainably, but the principle of having a Dawn who is massively better at combat than everyone else still applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T22:54:52-07:00","id":846951,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok 2ed. That makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:15:06-07:00","id":848946,"title":"","content":"Just had a thought vis-a-vis rolling ambushes: if you want your ambush strategies to be more effective, try house ruling that each character can only defend <i>themselves </i>with a successful application of Awareness. Technically, there is no rule stating whether or not a character can reflexively warn their party about an ambush to negate its effects. Though that's generally how I have run games in the past, perhaps simply shouting &quot;DANGER!&quot; isn't truly enough to negate the benefits of a well-timed and well-placed surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Some possible house rules:<br /> 1. Run on &quot;easy mode,&quot; where a single player can reflexively warn their party about imminent danger if they pass their Awareness check.<br /> 2. Passing an Awareness check reduces an Ambush to a Surprise Attack (-2 def instead of no defense and a free attack round) for everyone present.<br /> 3. Passing an Awareness check gives you enough time to warn one character about an enemy's location in detail, and/or declare Defend Other which negates the effects of ambush for that player.<br /> 4. Allow a successful Awareness check to negate or reduce the effects of an Ambush, but only with a stunt. Perhaps for a Minor stunt (+2 dice) you reduce the Ambush to a Surprise Attack, but for a Major stunt (+2 dice, +1 success and +1 willpower) you negate the effects altogether. Examples of the latter might include singing a song in a foreign language only the party understands that informs them discreetly of the ambush without letting your attackers know they've been made.<br /> <br /> Obviously not house rules for every table, but I for one have not ambushed a party of PCs in any system since my high school days. Someone ALWAYS brings a Notice/Awareness build to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:37:32-07:00","id":848991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=848946#post848946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just had a thought... perhaps simply shouting &quot;DANGER!&quot; isn't truly enough to negate the benefits of a well-timed and well-placed surprise attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Y'know, Sixteen, yelling 'Dodge!' is more distracting than helpful!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:03:16-07:00","id":858049,"title":"","content":"So just an update of sorts: I recently discovered that my party's Dawn had &quot;hacked the system&quot; a bit, taking physical stats as his tertiary stat block and dumping all his bonus points there at character gen to start with most or all of those stats at five (because it's cheaper to raise your tertiary stat block). Now, in a normal game this has the drawback of leaving no bonus points for your much-needed favored and caste abilities, but since we started as mortals who have no favored skills and pay two BP for all their ability dots, it was pretty much the one true build.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say this approach is &quot;wrong&quot; or even &quot;broken,&quot; but it's definitely a thing to be aware of moving forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:31:57-07:00","id":858109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858049#post858049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just an update of sorts: I recently discovered that my party's Dawn had &quot;hacked the system&quot; a bit, taking physical stats as his tertiary stat block and dumping all his bonus points there at character gen to start with most or all of those stats at five (because it's cheaper to raise your tertiary stat block). Now, in a normal game this has the drawback of leaving no bonus points for your much-needed favored and caste abilities, but since we started as mortals who have no favored skills and pay two BP for all their ability dots, it was pretty much the one true build.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say this approach is &quot;wrong&quot; or even &quot;broken,&quot; but it's definitely a thing to be aware of moving forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, I've thought about that before, but I dunno if it's actually a <i>good</i> build or just a fun one. It gives you better overall attributes, but often you don't really need more than a handful of dots in one of the three categories, and having to spend so much XP raising Abilties in the game (and being heavily constrained in your initial charm picks) is rough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:36:10-07:00","id":858111,"title":"","content":"Yeah, stuff like that isn't new. The particulars of that situation have exaggerated the effect of his min/maxing, but the underlying problem is that the game does a poor job of handling BP/XP incentives. It's a long-running gripe, the kind of thing that forumites come back to chew on every few months when things get slow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:36:43-07:00","id":858112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858109#post858109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha, I've thought about that before, but I dunno if it's actually a <i>good</i> build or just a fun one. It gives you better overall attributes, but often you don't really need more than a handful of dots in one of the three categories, and having to spend so much XP raising Abilties in the game (and being heavily constrained in your initial charm picks) is rough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah normally this would be a situational benefit at best, but because we started with mortals who don't get that nice BP cost break for favored abilities it was way more worth it. Really, I expect that the Lunar players are the ones who will abuse this loophole the most, if it's left open when that book comes out.<br /> <br /> Also, we're doing another combat-heavy game tomorrow night, so updates on what I tried and what worked or didn't work will be forthcoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:44:04-07:00","id":858114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858049#post858049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just an update of sorts: I recently discovered that my party's Dawn had &quot;hacked the system&quot; a bit, taking physical stats as his tertiary stat block and dumping all his bonus points there at character gen to start with most or all of those stats at five (because it's cheaper to raise your tertiary stat block).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why that's supposed to be hacking the system. Starting at 4 dots and spending 15 BPs to add 5 more leaves you with fewer physical dots than if you'd just put them as primary and then spent 12 BPs on buying 3 more. It gives you a more well-rounded character, since you have more dots in one of the other three categories, at the cost of being worse at the category that you're primarily focused on. If anything that's anti-optimisation, since min/maxing tends to be what leads to broken characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:45:01-07:00","id":858115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858109#post858109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha, I've thought about that before, but I dunno if it's actually a <i>good</i> build or just a fun one. It gives you better overall attributes, but often you don't really need more than a handful of dots in one of the three categories, and having to spend so much XP raising Abilties in the game (and being heavily constrained in your initial charm picks) is rough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. The first couple dots of a Favored or Caste Ability is one of the most cost-efficient uses of XP in the game, and lots of entry-level combat Charms have low Ability minimums (he is a Dawn, remember). He can pour XP into those areas while relying on high Attributes to shore up his dice pools in the short run, and in the long run he'll have higher pools and dice caps in his physical areas than he would otherwise since he won't have to pay punishing costs to raise his Attributes with XP later on. Any short term pain will disappear very quickly, and long term he'll probably be better off since the alternative would have been paying 2BP per dot to raise an Ability to 5.<br /> <br /> It's not just a good build. Given the circumstances it was almost certainly the optimal one. It probably<i> shouldn't</i> be, but it <i>is</i>. Like I said, not a new problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:50:06-07:00","id":858120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858114#post858114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure why that's supposed to be hacking the system. Starting at 4 dots and spending 15 BPs to add 5 more leaves you with fewer physical dots than if you'd just put them as primary and then spent 12 BPs on buying 3 more. It gives you a more well-rounded character, since you have more dots in one of the other three categories, at the cost of being worse at the category that you're primarily focused on. If anything that's anti-optimisation, since min/maxing tends to be what leads to broken characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes another dot in a Primary is worth more than another dot in a Secondary or Tertiary. That's a flawed assumption. Physical stats are not the only ones relevant to a character, or even to combat. Wits leaps readily to mind. If all the player cared about doing is getting as many Physical traits as he could then you'd be right, but there's more to optimization than being the beefiest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:08:35-07:00","id":858147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858115#post858115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah. The first couple dots of a Favored or Caste Ability is one of the most cost-efficient uses of XP in the game, and lots of entry-level combat Charms have low Ability minimums (he is a Dawn, remember). He can pour XP into those areas while relying on high Attributes to shore up his dice pools in the short run, and in the long run he'll have higher pools and dice caps in his physical areas than he would otherwise since he won't have to pay punishing costs to raise his Attributes with XP later on. Any short term pain will disappear very quickly, and long term he'll probably be better off since the alternative would have been paying 2BP per dot to raise an Ability to 5.<br /> <br /> It's not just a good build. Given the circumstances it was almost certainly the optimal one. It probably<i> shouldn't</i> be, but it <i>is</i>. Like I said, not a new problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Spending 15 bps on boosting your tertiary attributes is worth between 44xp and 64xp.<br /> Buying 3 unfavoured (as that's the only option) dots up to 5, one to 4, and a specialty, would be worth 51xp. About the same really. Even once those abilities all magically become favoured after Exaltation, that's still worth 44xp anyway. So I wouldn't say it's the optimal build, it's about the same.<br /> And he'd have min-maxier stats if he put primary physical and also had combat stats at 5.<br /> <br /> While you are right that all attributes are sometimes relevant to combat, physical attributes are a lot <i>more</i> relevant to combat. Having Str 3, Dex 5, Sta 3, Melee 5, Thrown 5, Athletics 5, Awareness 4 and specialty in spears (for example) is going to be better than Str 4, Dex 5, Sta 3, Melee 3, Thrown 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 3.<br /> <br /> Honestly, with 9 in physical stats, 6 in social and 8 in mental... he's probably a more well-rounded character, so I think that has probably worked out well!<br /> <br /> Also, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first couple dots of a Favored or Caste Ability is one of the most cost-efficient uses of XP in the game </div> </div> </div> Sorry, I don't quite understand what you mean here? You have to start with the first dot of your Favoured ability, so you're not spending XP on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-03-2016, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:12:30-07:00","id":858148,"title":"","content":"From the math I'm seeing here, it sounds like he found a way to be a strong all-rounder at character gen instead of having to pick one field and max it out. It's... actually somewhat nice that this option exists? Because it didn't really in Ex2. So, maybe a pretty beneficial hack all told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:16:40-07:00","id":858152,"title":"","content":"That's how it looks to me.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I like that the tertiary attributes are cheaper, because in 2nd ed you'd rarely want to buy any attributes anyway, but if you did you'd definitely only buy primary attributes.<br /> For the Solar character I recently made, I did actually buy Wits 4 (she has Perception and Intelligence 2) for 3 bps. 4 bps would have been too pricey (since it's only 12xp). Mostly, it'd be too pricey because you have 15 bps. So after you've bought 6 abilities to 5, you've got 3bps left, so why not buy up your tertiary attribute that's at 3 or 4 up by 1?<br /> (I know it's more optimal to buy 7 abilities to 5, but after 6 I just didn't have more I wanted that high).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-03-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:37:59-07:00","id":858162,"title":"","content":"I love it because my usual stat breakdown for characters has me dumping all my tertiary points into one attribute and sinking two (like bringing Wits up to 5 for fighters) or bringing two up to three and dumping one. I know it's more effective to buy those up with XP later, but sometimes I like starting off at average Intelligence instead of role-playing being dumb as a rock at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:41:17-07:00","id":858166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858115#post858115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah. The first couple dots of a Favored or Caste Ability is one of the most cost-efficient uses of XP in the game, and lots of entry-level combat Charms have low Ability minimums (he is a Dawn, remember). He can pour XP into those areas while relying on high Attributes to shore up his dice pools in the short run, and in the long run he'll have higher pools and dice caps in his physical areas than he would otherwise since he won't have to pay punishing costs to raise his Attributes with XP later on. Any short term pain will disappear very quickly, and long term he'll probably be better off since the alternative would have been paying 2BP per dot to raise an Ability to 5.<br /> <br /> It's not just a good build. Given the circumstances it was almost certainly the optimal one. It probably<i> shouldn't</i> be, but it <i>is</i>. Like I said, not a new problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, it's a very fun, interesting build, but I'm pretty sure it's not at all optimal for an Ability Exalt. The issue is that nobody really <i>needs </i>the kind of uniformly huge Attributes this build creates, and an optimizer wouldn't generally shoot for them except for how temptingly cheap the tertiaries are, so you would typically not be doing that with your XP in the first place. Hence, comparing the XP cost of raising Attributes to that level rather than raising Abilities is a bit of a red herring, because under normal circumstances you'd just pick Physical primary, dump one or two stats of little value to you in your other categories (which are much more dump-friendly) to ensure you have good ratings in the things that matter, and then not do much to raise Attributes after that. From the sounds of it, this character ended up with around 34 dots in Attributes, which is almost unheard of -- nobody without Attribute charms takes their Attributes that high with XP because it's just not really worth it. Hence, figuring out how much it would cost to get them to that level in play isn't terribly informative. I'm not much of a bean-counter, but if you're going to bean-count it only really makes sense in terms of some hypothetical end-state build you plan to converge on regardless of what you look like in chargen.<br /> <br /> Bear with me a moment.<br /> <br /> Let's say you hope to end up with three fives and two fours in your Abilities, which is a pretty realistic middle-of-the-road spread for an experienced Solar. If you start with all those things at 3, that's 46 XP. Unlike the huge attribute build, you probably will actually want to get these dots one way or another, since they're prerequisites for things. If you got those 8 dots in chargen, it'd cost 16 BP, so the optimization question is: what can you do with your Attributes for 5 BP and 46 XP?<br /> <br /> From the way this was described (and looking at it from an bean-counting optimization standpoint), I'm going to suppose this person is 5/5/4 physical, 5/5/1 primary, 5/3/1 secondary, where the ratings are assigned however you want within categories. It might not be exactly that, but that's the &quot;best&quot; setup from a purely bean-counting perspective. Now, if you put physical primary and don't put any BP in Attributes just yet, you end up with 5/5/1 physical, 5/3/1 secondary, 5/1/1 tertiary.<br /> <br /> Put 4 BP into raising your secondary 3 to a 4. Spend the last BP on, I guess, a Merit dot, since what else can you do with 1 BP with no Favored Abilities? At this point, if you wanted to get up to 5/5/4, 5/5/1, 5/3/1 it would cost you 52 XP, which is indeed a little more -- more than is offset by the extra Merit dot, at least. But let's say you stop at 5/5/4, 5/5/1, 5/2/1. That's 44 XP. Do you <i>really</i> want that one extra attribute dot in your least-important attribute category more than anything else you could get for 8 Solar XP? I can't see it -- in practice, most people would stop at much lower Attributes if they were buying them in play, so it looks to me like those sales that encourage you to &quot;save&quot; money by spending it on something you don't really want. Even the 6-XP advantage shown here evaporates quickly if you aren't willing to stomach the two Attributes at one.<br /> <br /> This is probably kind of a long digression for me to get into given my well-known antipathy toward bean-counting. But I just really like math problems.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: </i>Actually, I'm a bit daft here -- you can still do better than what I posted. On Abilities, just get the three fives for 12 BP, buy the secondary Attribute 3 to a 5, then use your XP to buy the two Ability 4s and the remaining 5 attribute dots, and that actually gets you to the exact same end state for <i>precisely</i> the same amount of XP, except you have one extra merit dot. Optimization! It's stupid but fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-03-2016, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:25:27-07:00","id":858184,"title":"","content":"It always amuses me when people conflate &quot;optimized character&quot; with &quot;hyper-focused character&quot; as though the two are the same rather than coincidental states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:00:45-07:00","id":858191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858184#post858184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always amuses me when people conflate &quot;optimized character&quot; with &quot;hyper-focused character&quot; as though the two are the same rather than coincidental states.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that in gaming as a whole this is generally done because you get more for investing heavily in one thing than modestly in several things, but in Exalted it's due to the quadratic XP costing and the high value of 5s. Practically speaking, of course, the most important thing about any optimization problem is what you're choosing to optimize for. But that's more or less the kind of optimization you were talking about, right? The benefit of going the all-attributes-at-chargen route in terms of XP cost to reach a given end state is less the less hyper-focused you were. I could rework the example to assume a more naturalistic spread of dots, but it'd probably make that setup look even worse from a bean-counting perspective, which is why I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T09:35:11-07:00","id":858371,"title":"","content":"Hi, dawn caste here. With the mortal creation rules it is a bit more tempting, specifically that you have 21 bonus points and a stat spread of 6/4/3 putting physical as my tertiary and spending all my BP on it changed it to 10/6/4. Since I had no favored skills and it would be 2 BP each for those I can say it was really nice having dex and stamina 5 with a solid strength for my gunzosha commando while still being able to have wits 5. With the benifits of exaltation I ended up with a stat spread of 11/8/6 which puts almost every stat I use at 5 (strength is still at 4 and intelegence I am upping slowly with xp but otherwise I don't need to worry about them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","user":"korekore","date":". 04-03-2016, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:25:02-07:00","id":858393,"title":"","content":"You got 21 bonus points and then with exaltation you got the same amount of stats as a normal starting Solar?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:30:25-07:00","id":858396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858393#post858393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got 21 bonus points and then with exaltation you got the same amount of stats as a normal starting Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the rules as written on page 125 of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","user":"korekore","date":". 04-03-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:31:22-07:00","id":858447,"title":"","content":"I confess I never understood this &quot;give mortals less dots to distribute, but more bonus points&quot; that has existed since way back in the storyteller games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:05:05-07:00","id":858511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858447#post858447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess I never understood this &quot;give mortals less dots to distribute, but more bonus points&quot; that has existed since way back in the storyteller games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is to encourage anime tropes with the mechanics for Exalts. In anime, characters often have that &quot;one thing&quot; they do better than anyone alive while being laughably incompetent at everything else, re: the super tech genius who can't cook, the martial artist who gets lost for days in cities, the stealth master who never speaks because they can't carry on a conversation, etc. The rules for generating exalts encourage these tropes by heavily favoring min-maxing, but maybe they want mortals to seem more &quot;real&quot; by making all skills and attributes about equally difficult to level. It still benefits you to max your stats out at char gen, but at two BP an ability dot players are more willing to experiment with stuff like this as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:14:07-07:00","id":858520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858184#post858184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always amuses me when people conflate &quot;optimized character&quot; with &quot;hyper-focused character&quot; as though the two are the same rather than coincidental states.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really a coincidence if it happens over and over again?<br /> <br /> There are a lot of games that reward hyperfocus. And it's easy to see why; if improving the abilities you intend to use often costs the same amount as improving the ones you intend to use rarely, focusing heavily is usually gonna be optimal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:53:33-07:00","id":858541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858511#post858511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is to encourage anime tropes with the mechanics for Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just a repetition of way older Storyteller rules, though. I doubt Vampire: The Masquerade was trying to encourage anime tropes, yet Vampires have 15 BP and mortals have 21 BP with less dots all around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:12:22-07:00","id":858586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858447#post858447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess I never understood this &quot;give mortals less dots to distribute, but more bonus points&quot; that has existed since way back in the storyteller games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually makes sense in Exalted, since you need to pay a lot more for Ability dots as a mortal, so I guess it was an idea waiting for its time. I dunno what the rationale was in older games, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:45:24-07:00","id":858603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858586#post858586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually makes sense in Exalted, since you need to pay a lot more for Ability dots as a mortal, so I guess it was an idea waiting for its time. I dunno what the rationale was in older games, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess that works. Though a fringe strangeness remains in that mortals get (if both &quot;sides&quot; are putting nearly every BP into it) more Merits than Solars, who presumably have an easier time accumulating power, wealth and influence or developing amazing physical qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:35:30-07:00","id":858627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=858603#post858603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though a fringe strangeness remains in that mortals get (if both &quot;sides&quot; are putting nearly every BP into it) more Merits than Solars, who presumably have an easier time accumulating power, wealth and influence or developing amazing physical qualities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be intentional. Consider this. In a mortals game, you're generally not trying to run PCs who are average even if they're mortals. More Merit dots means your mortal PCs are easily princes, spymasters, Guild caravan-masters, mercenary company commanders, Realm patricians, scavenger-lords, Threshold generals, etc. A cut above the chaff of normal people, even as mortals.<br /> <br /> Exalted are clearly special and a cut above by virtue of the magic they gain access to, both active and passive. For mortals, many of whom as PCs may not have a 5 in an Ability, starting with Resources 5 is a bigger deal than for a Solar, and in a lot of ways, much easier for a Solar to acquire in play than a mortal.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure how that's strange. Exalted, for free, get a slew of bonuses that mortals either have to pay Merits for to kind-of replicate, or flat out cannot buy. You're seeing some kind of competition where there isn't any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:57:25-07:00","id":858696,"title":"","content":"It is unlikely to come up since it would be rare for anyone to invest all or almost all of their BP on Merits, and it is not a big deal since the final difference is at most 2 dots, but it still fact that, say, a mortal emperor or something could start the game with Resources 5, Influence 5, Command 5 x2, Backing 3, Allies 1 x2, Contacts 2 or whatever other combination in that sense of being rich and influential and a Solar emperor couldn't.<br /> <br /> The fact that Solars have a bunch of massive advantages and will be obviously superior anyway is the reason that the small strangeness of &quot;huh, isn't it curious how mortals can end up with more merits than Solars?&quot; is actually strange to me. Because &quot;Mr. Temporal Power, the Solar&quot;, by dint of all those advantages, would be plenty capable of getting all those merits.<br /> <br /> Which, again, is unlikely to matter and not a big deal if it does. But it <i>is</i> there and I <i>do</i> find it weird. It is not like there is not plenty of other weirdness in Exalted chargen, historically: 2E Solars, Abyssals, Infernals and Lunars having the same* chargen whatever their education and backstory, while DBs get better chargen if Dynasts and Sidereals get better chargen if not Ronin. All the woes people have with BP/XP disparities. Or how there was mechanical incentive to &quot;optimize your personality&quot; with Virtues. And so on.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you don't mind I'd rather drop this tangent - you let me find strangeness wherever I want, I let you find not strangeness wherever you want and the thread can go back to challenging those Dragons-damned full Solar Circles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Except for access to mechanically superior backgrounds in some cases. But that usually came with substantial in-setting complications</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T02:27:12-07:00","id":858844,"title":"","content":"So we had to wrap up before finishing the combat tonight, but here is what I pitched at my Dawn and here is what happened:<br /> <br /> I built a Full Moon Lunar soak-health beast hoping to create something that would at least last a couple rounds with him. He has better soak than Octavian: 11 from artifact heavy armor, 5 from Stamina, and +4 for his war form, for a total soak of 20 which is what my Dawn has. He has 28 Health levels, 14 of which are -4s. He wields a Dire Lance (Heavy Artifact, Piercing, Reaching) and rolls eleven dice to hit, with +23 raw damage (another +4 for its war form). His Parry is five. He has all Physical attributes and melee/brawl at five. He rides a stat-boosted Hellboar, which is also his totem animal, and gains all of its creature powers in war form. I gave him <i>several</i> of Octavian's powers for good measure but halved their mote cost to account for his smaller mote pool.<br /> <br /> Here is what happened:<br /> <br /> My Dawn got 22 on his join battle roll to my Lunar's 18. My Dawn rides an upgraded Simhatta (son of the Simhatta god) and they both rushed each other and clashed on round one. Both are using the charm Seasoned Beast-Rider's Approach and roll their mounts into combat on their tick. My Lunar gets 18 to hit on the clash but my Dawn rolls 20+, then does 14 withering damage. The Simhatta also wins the clash and does substantial withering damage, but does not crash the Hellboar. The Lunar and Hellboar continue charging past the Dawn, aiming for the nearby town of soft targets. So the Simhatta gives chase and uses a willpower to reflexively attack again with decisive damage, killing the Hellboar in a single strike. My Dawn then activated Peony Blossom Attack, striking at the Lunar for the second time that turn. The Lunar attempted to react with Invincible Iron Bastion and a full excellency, but Parry 13 did not defend it from an attack with 21 successes. The Dawn did a total of 14 decisive damage, putting the Lunar just barely into its -4s in round one. However, my Lunar activated The Tower Still Stands, putting him back at 16 initiative. Both fighters are now unmounted, as the Solar lept off his mount to deliver that blow (SBRA allows you to do this).<br /> <br /> And that's where we ended. Here are my most important take aways:<br /> <br /> 1: Never underestimate the benefits of a reflexive decisive attack. With a good Join Battle Roll and a good Withering hit you can get all the Initiative you need to kill <i>most</i> things in this game, and being able to follow that with a Decisive attack on the<i> same turn</i> before losing any of it to withering ripostes is a big deal.<br /> <br /> 2: Defense alone will not save you from charm-users. I had a really big boost going to my Lunar's Parry, more than any excellency could give, and it was still not nearly enough to combat an attack with a full excellency and Excellent Strike. Honestly I feel like the motes I spent boosting his Parry were just wasted. 7+ Defense might save you from most things but don't expect it to hold up against a combat specialist.<br /> <br /> 3: Those extra levels from Ox-Body are so worth it. Obviously this is an extreme example, but if I'm able to turn this fight around at all next game it will only be because my Lunar survived a hit that should have killed them and now has enough initiative to counter attack a Solar who has only seven health levels, which brings me to my last point:<br /> <br /> 4: Having another way to build initiative in a fight is indeed a must. It was suggested earlier here and I will testify, if not for The Tower Still Stands my Lunar would still have less initiative than my Dawn and surviving that first hit would just mean dragging this fight out for another round. Hopefully I can crash my Dawn next game, and then we'll see how effectively a well-made fighter can come back from crash.<br /> <br /> There are many things this Lunar has not used yet that I am looking forward to testing in their fight in two weeks. Not least of which is the fact that he actually functions better at his -4 health levels, but no more on that here on a thread my players might be reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-04-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:13:42-07:00","id":859312,"title":"","content":"Yeah I can see how this system is <i>faster </i>than previous eds', but that write-up sure doesn't feel any more <i>satisfying</i>.<br /> <br /> One-shots can be cool when they feel like they accomplished something, or where you just get to clearly display your prowess above and beyond some foe, but from one familiar into another, it just feels...cheap? Sad? And from my experiences and the the experiences I've been reading, the system easily boils down to JB rocket tag, even with defenses. Ehhh.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:54:33-07:00","id":859328,"title":"","content":"So...the Dawn player rolled 22 successes on JB, then 20+ successes on an attack roll, then 14 withering damage (against an enemy with 19 Soak), then 21 successes on a Decisive attack, then 14 decisive damage on 37 dice. Even taking into account the effect of maxed dice pools, Charms, Clash bonuses, and stunts he is beating the odds on every roll. I don't think I would be too eager to draw broad conclusions about the soundness of the system from what appears to be a statistical outlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T22:28:40-07:00","id":859469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859328#post859328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...the Dawn player rolled 22 successes on JB, then 20+ successes on an attack roll, then 14 withering damage (against an enemy with 19 Soak), then 21 successes on a Decisive attack, then 14 decisive damage on 37 dice. Even taking into account the effect of maxed dice pools, Charms, Clash bonuses, and stunts he is beating the odds on every roll. I don't think I would be too eager to draw broad conclusions about the soundness of the system from what appears to be a statistical outlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is our fifth session and I can tell you that he's been rolling like this all game. Even as a mortal he rolled 15+ successes with great regularity. On most attack rolls he is getting at least a level two stunt and spending willpower in addition to using a full excellency and Excellent Strike, but I think that's about it. At a certain point, it stops being a fluke and becomes something you need to start planning for.<br /> <br /> I don't think that there is a problem with the system, but as the thread title insinuates it is often hard to even <i>challenge</i> Solar exalts when they are in their element like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T23:37:09-07:00","id":859492,"title":"","content":"Are you playing on Roll20? Or using any other online die rolling API like an IRC bot? If so, I think your party dawn is rolling like this: Xd10&lt;7; instead of this, which is how he should be rolling: Xd10&gt;7. The die rolls you're claiming are too incredible to be a coincidence, and an inverted greater than sign easily accounts for it, especially if you're counting 10s manually on top of that. The sorts of success totals that you're claiming on pretty much every roll are tremendously unlikely when playing normally. I've only seen numbers like that very rarely over the course of multiple games of Exalted 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","user":"nihnoz","date":". 04-05-2016, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T07:25:39-07:00","id":859633,"title":"","content":"It isn't actually possible for someone to be consistently lucky. If he consistently rolls higher than the odds would indicate, and this effect is repeatable, something wrong is happening. Maybe cheating, maybe carelessness.<br /> <br /> Also, players are generally only supposed to get two or three two-point stunts per session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T08:20:29-07:00","id":859661,"title":"","content":"As the dawn I can give some extra insight to these. The join battle roll was the luckiest I have had statistically as it was 16 dice with 1 auto success and double 9. The attack roll was a major stunt (which I get on most attacks) with full excellency use and wp use putting it at 25 dice (med weapon with specialty) and 4 auto successes with reroll 1's. The second attack roll was similar save it was a decisive attack so a few dice less rolled. These were still good rolls but the damage roll was about average on the first hit and below on the second which is why I may go down next round. In the pre game it is also worth noting we thought a wp added 3 dice with skewed things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T08:44:19-07:00","id":859670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859469#post859469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that there is a problem with the system, but as the thread title insinuates it is often hard to even <i>challenge</i> Solar exalts when they are in their element like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's that hard to provide meaningful challenges to the basic/most popular character type I would absolutely say it's a problem with the system. <br /> <br /> Some people may not see it as a problem what with Solars being awesome and such. For me, games where I'm not challenged and don't have to think, don't interest me. If you can hammer the Chsrm buttons and win without really trying or without consequence for using your motes, that's a systemic problem. <br /> <br /> Now I'm not entirely sure that's what's happening in this case because 1 on 1s obviously favor Solars, but there are enough threads about Solars 1 shotting large battlegroups and then DBs leading them that I'm not convinced it's a fluke. I haven't seen much on the flip side either. You shouldn't have to throw 2 Octavians at a group in order to make the characters break a sweat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:26:05-07:00","id":859691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859670#post859670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 Octavians</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the time a friend killed two Hive Tyrants in one attack in a game of Deathwatch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:14:14-07:00","id":859720,"title":"","content":"In the games I've been in, Dawns being able to One-Two kill enemies by spending a crap-ton of essence has been a massive problem. It's at the point where I'm honestly considering giving every even moderately important villain a perfect or two because I'm sick of the Brawl-Dawn being able to throw a single massively-boosted withering to crash someone, then heaven-thunder-hammer OHKO them the next turn, or the Melee Dawn rolling 30+ successes because they dropped a full excellency with a single WP, tossed excellent strike on it, boosted with Rising Sun Slash. It's so much easier to boost offense that without a perfect, you just absolutely can't avoid being hit if someone really wants to hit you. I'm at the point where I'm looking forward to a lower power level for the DB book just so I can write challenging antagonists without everyone being a full circle of experienced exalts or a 5000 man army of multiple high-size elite drill battlegroups led by dragonblooded commanders.<br /> <br /> Edit: And this kind of reckless mote expenditure would be a lot easier to punish if they would actually end the combat without a single mote left, but regenerating 5 per turn means they can utterly melt the threatening combatant easily turn 1 or 2, then play it safe and top off the fuel-tank against the other opponents. I've had people go from almost empty peripheral to full personal in a combat because they just stood back at a safe distance and plinked with arrows or gathered SM to do some big spell-damage without spending any motes, while scary melee combatants couldn't reach them because the Dawn was beefy enough to prevent any disengaging. <br /> <br /> Really my biggest problem isn't that I'm unable to write a challenging antagonist; I could! I could toss Octavian-tier statlines at them any time I wanted a challenging fight, but the problem is justifying that every time. And I can't even use the threat of the Wyld Hunt coming down because so far, all these combats have been in isolated locations/no witnessess/no witnesses that would spill the beans about a few Anathema going hog-wild on an Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","user":"Grindavikur","date":". 04-05-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:26:33-07:00","id":859733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859720#post859720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...means they can utterly melt the threatening combatant easily turn 1 or 2, then play it safe and top off the fuel-tank against the other opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first suggested solution is to stop telegraphing who the most threatening combatant is. Set up the pushover as the big bad, and have his wussy toady in fact be the one with the devastating power. Let the party unleash on the riff-raff so they are less prepared for the true threat. This suggestion only works based on the strategies your party seems to be following.<br /> <br /> Alternately, use a big battle-group between the threatening guy and the party. It's not particularly easy to move through a battle-group, and that gives your big-bad a round or two of free ranged time (or possibly spell-casting time. Magma Kraken anybody?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:55:48-07:00","id":859790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not going to condemn the <i>system </i>for enemies getting wtfpwned when it sounds like their entire strategy is to strike a menacing pose in front of a circle of Solar Exalts and then raise their hands for a cracking bout of fisticuffs. Opponents who play by schoolyard rules get bulldozed by PCs who don't. Also, if part of the problem is players going hog-wild with no consequences then maybe, I dunno, have there be some consequences?<br /> <br /> Also as an aside HTH is hilariously OP. I thought that was obvious by now, but maybe it's not? Seriously, that shit is over the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:02:25-07:00","id":859856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859670#post859670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's that hard to provide meaningful challenges to the basic/most popular character type I would absolutely say it's a problem with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I don't think this is a problem with the <i>mechanics</i> so much as the antagonists in the back of the book being severely under-powered. This has been a systemic problem with all the White Wolf and Onyx Path franchises since VtM; I assume it stems from the developers not wanting to alienate their player-base by making the game &quot;too hard&quot; for newbies, but the end result is that there are really only three things in that whole section that will make a Dawn break a sweat. Part of what I hope to accomplish with this thread in the long-term is coming up with strategies for &quot;boosting&quot; those canon stats so that STs and players hoping for a real challenge will be able to get it.<br /> <br /> Now having said that, there <i>were</i> improvements this edition. Animals in Ex2 were usually joke antagonists, but now with creature powers not only am I finding that things like Great Cats are fun to field and play, but almost everyone in my party took a familiar background. As much as I think we shouldn't have to go this far out to find a worthy foe at Essence 1, Octavian, Ahlat and the Nephwracks <i>do</i> represent real obstacles to a Solar exalt, and can be used as blueprints for antagonists that you want to have a real punch. I also suspect that Fakharu would give my Dawn pause, but I haven't tested out any of his charmset yet. Maybe next session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859733#post859733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first suggested solution is to stop telegraphing who the most threatening combatant is. Set up the pushover as the big bad, and have his wussy toady in fact be the one with the devastating power. Let the party unleash on the riff-raff so they are less prepared for the true threat. This suggestion only works based on the strategies your party seems to be following.<br /> <br /> Alternately, use a big battle-group between the threatening guy and the party. It's not particularly easy to move through a battle-group, and that gives your big-bad a round or two of free ranged time (or possibly spell-casting time. Magma Kraken anybody?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also finding that the traditional &quot;dungeon crawl&quot; game works well for breaking down a party's mote pools. Out-of-combat traps and short encounters with low-level monsters offer a great opportunity to make your party burn their motes on excellencies without giving them time to rest and get those motes back in hour-long real-time regeneration. I did this for their first exalt-tier fight and it almost worked, but they had just enough essence left to one-shot the boss who they found much earlier than anticipated. Had I thrown an extra minion encounter in there, I think that fight would have been very different.<br /> <br /> What I'm generally finding is that my players use way more than five motes per turn, and quickly burn through their pools when faced with boss-type characters. I'm hoping this might be the fight where I get to test the system after both parties are running on their 5m per turn drip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-05-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:04:02-07:00","id":859908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859790#post859790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not going to condemn the <i>system </i>for enemies getting wtfpwned when it sounds like their entire strategy is to strike a menacing pose in front of a circle of Solar Exalts and then raise their hands for a cracking bout of fisticuffs. Opponents who play by schoolyard rules get bulldozed by PCs who don't. Also, if part of the problem is players going hog-wild with no consequences then maybe, I dunno, have there be some consequences?<br /> <br /> Also as an aside HTH is hilariously OP. I thought that was obvious by now, but maybe it's not? Seriously, that shit is over the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most fights have been structured with multiple opponents trying to drag down the party. One had a single E3 Abyssal swordsman backed up by multiple buffed-up War-Ghosts and another, lower essence Abyssal focused on buffing all the others with Nightingale and performance. That one actually had a good amount of back and forth, but that had build-up; I can't justify that tier of threat every single time there's a combat. We've had one major fight where it was enduring a siege of undead creatures, stitched together titans, cannons, etc. Others were chases through the forest with very pissed off Lunars and elemental servants.<br /> <br /> Mostly my problems with players spending all their motes have been in situations where social manipulators/vagaries of the story allowed for there to be any kind of duel. We've also had fights where players have bursted their motepools until they're in danger of flaring, essentially &quot;tagged in&quot; another circle-mate (we have 2 Dawns) to take the brunt of the threat until they've filled up more, switch off, etc. As a result, we've only had each character flare once a piece, and they always did so in situations where that wouldn't logically send warning bells to every Dragonblooded for a thousand miles.<br /> <br /> And while I don't have a problem with my players succeeding when they lay out plans, follow them, deal with complications and wrinkles, and finish things without anyone but dead enemies having seen them exercise supernatural skill. My problem is that I'm having such a hard time plotting out more than a few TYPES of difficult combats when we have a Melee Dawn who can passively sit at 7 defense before charms, a thrown/awareness/stealth dawn who's pulped more than a few foes with a sneaky Steel-Storm/Joint-Wounding...If I write up people who have an answer to their incredibly strong specializations EVERY TIME that cheapens both of their skillsets. People with such high awareness makes ambushes nigh-impossible. People with such high passive defenses make writing the monster who has low dex and high strength a waste of time and turns. People with incredibly high round-one-damage potential (Cough. Thrown. Couch) make writing antagonists without a perfect/without some crazy resistance charms not a smart idea.<br /> <br /> Again, I can write out combatants who can challenge these characters. It's not a matter of me not knowing how to write an intelligent villain, or a threatening combatant, it's justifying it all the time, and justifying them being strong against what the players are good at every time. If players are being sneaky, I can't just bring five old immaculate masters who know who they're hunting. So uh. &quot;Menacing pose in front of the circle and raise their hands&quot;...Has actually only happened once, and that was the honorable (in his own way) E3 Abyssal who challenged them the most by virtue of being a singularly terrifying combatant purpose-built to be a wakeup call. Multi-attacks, counters, resistance charms that let him one-time negate the Thrown Users habit of absurdly strong SSDs...But I can't have every antagonist be built like that.<br /> <br /> I might try in the future to force wedges in that split the party more often, so they can't cover each others weaknesses/the thrown character with high awareness can't prevent ambushes/etc, but I'll need to be careful so it doesn't make them decide to just get glued together at the hip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859856#post859856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also finding that the traditional &quot;dungeon crawl&quot; game works well for breaking down a party's mote pools. Out-of-combat traps and short encounters with low-level monsters offer a great opportunity to make your party burn their motes on excellencies without giving them time to rest and get those motes back in hour-long real-time regeneration. I did this for their first exalt-tier fight and it almost worked, but they had just enough essence left to one-shot the boss who they found much earlier than anticipated. Had I thrown an extra minion encounter in there, I think that fight would have been very different.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I might also try this! We already had a case of a back-to-back combat where the fight with the Abyssal, who chunked 8 HL from the Thrown Dawn and 3 HL from the Melee Dawn with one multiattack, and brought both Dawns pretty low on motes and the Sorcerer Twilight to no stored up motes from rituals, was then immediately followed by the undead army showing up. Unfortunately, the undead titans didn't have the accuracy to hit the melee user, and her athletics were high enough that she was able to pin them with my discovery of the weirdness of Disengages for creatures with Legendary Size. S'why I made the thread about possible houserules for that a bit ago. But yeah, more cases where it's immediately apparent that chunking people with supernova mote usage is a bad idea through obvious fights that will come very soon after/some cases where there's a bait and switch antagonist to make them waste all their motes/one-use abilities on one target will definitely be used. Thanks for the advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","user":"Grindavikur","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:10:01-07:00","id":859913,"title":"","content":"You can't have every antagonist be capable of threatening a Solar circle because pretty much nothing <i>is</i> capable of threatening a Solar circle. Big dramatic showdowns that can threaten the lives of a Dawn and their Solar buddies should be very rare, climactic events, not a regular occurrence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:27:14-07:00","id":859926,"title":"","content":"I'm fully aware of that, but when I DO want there to be a challenging fight, it's annoying that I'm pigeonholed into very specific methods of creating a challenging fight due to the sheer mechanical power of the Dawns tricks/the power of &quot;I'll just spend all my motes this round and the next and the big scary nation-shattering monster with 30 HL is going to evaporate into a red mist&quot;. Yes, everyone likes to say that it's not about stopping the circle from doing something, but dealing with the consequences of it, but if you're going to go down that route then why have a combat system at all? Especially this big and complex of one. I'm also searching for a middle-ground between climactic fights with powerful abyssals, incredibly ancient ghosts, full complements of Wyld Hunt Shikari...and the fights where I don't even roll dice and just tell the Exalts &quot;Well you've stepped in to save this poor defenseless man from ten bandits. Describe how you shame these men in combat.&quot; More fights where, no, they're not at risk of dying, but they are at risk of at least taking a health-level or two so no one can say &quot;Isn't it funny we haven't lost a single Health Level in the last 10 combats?&quot; (Something I actually said in a campaign I was a player in, not a GM. Had a very heavily focused Brawl-Dawn and my experiences with him convinced me that future characters of mine should be a lot less specialized to give the GM more opportunities to challenge me/the rest of the party)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Something Kindled pointed out that I almost forgot. This kind of difficulty in writing antagonists is happening for a circle of Essence 1 (Now partially into E2) Solars. A handful of E1 Solars aren't anything to sneeze at, yeah, but they're still only Essence 1. If you'd make the argument that a full circle of E5 Solars should almost never feel actual fear to their personal wellbeing, yes, I'd 100% agree. It's HARD to scare a bunch of elder exalts. But fresh whelps recently Exalted? It should be a lot easier to put the fear of flashiness in them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","user":"Grindavikur","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:47:00-07:00","id":859938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859913#post859913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't have every antagonist be capable of threatening a Solar circle because pretty much nothing <i>is</i> capable of threatening a Solar circle. Big dramatic showdowns that can threaten the lives of a Dawn and their Solar buddies should be very rare, climactic events, not a regular occurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the flipside, having 9 out of every 10 fights just total curb stomps that really aren't worth taking the time to play out because the outcome is painfully obvious, is fucking boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:58:10-07:00","id":859945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859856#post859856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I don't think this is a problem with the <i>mechanics</i> so much as the antagonists in the back of the book being severely under-powered. This has been a systemic problem with all the White Wolf and Onyx Path franchises since VtM; I assume it stems from the developers not wanting to alienate their player-base by making the game &quot;too hard&quot; for newbies, but the end result is that there are really only three things in that whole section that will make a Dawn break a sweat. Part of what I hope to accomplish with this thread in the long-term is coming up with strategies for &quot;boosting&quot; those canon stats so that STs and players hoping for a real challenge will be able to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game could definitely use more elder Exalted QCs with heft, but on the whole, I'm a little skeptical that the answer is to buff the antagonists. A lot of the disparity seems to be the result of how obscenely strong a devoted combat-supernal character can get, but a mid-range combatant with 4-6 dice in their combat pools and two combat charms is supposed to be fun to play in a fight, so if you make it so the former type of character is routinely given a tough time, the latter is going to get slaughtered without a constant tanking escort, and then the game veers toward everyone taking extremely combat-focused builds because they &quot;have&quot; to, which annoys the people who didn't want to build that way, and annoys the actual combat monkeys because they're too similar to everybody else.<br /> <br /> I think this is a more structural flaw with the way the game is than perhaps people are giving it credit for. A Solar already starts out as among the best of the best in the thing they're good at, which has the perverse effect of reducing its ability to be an engaging challenge for them. The problem you are running into isn't actually any worse than what happens if you try to run a mystery for a heavily-invested Investigation Supernal character, or naval obstacles at a heavily-invested Sail Supernal character, or what have you.<br /> <br /> If you think about it from a setting angle, doesn't it seem like a Melee Supernal Dawn with max or near-max combat stats and a heavy investment in Melee Charms <i>should</i> be able to dispatch most other powerful supernatural warriors easily? Is that not the whole idea of the Dawn Caste, and the destabilizing threat of Solar excellence? If you uplift more than a handful of the greatest adversaries to the point where they're seriously threatening rather than simply having some shot at winning or surviving, doesn't that seem like it's short-selling the whole idea of the legend of war returned from death who shakes the world to its foundations, which is implicitly what someone wants to play when they design a character like that? Moreover, shouldn't a Solar swashbuckler with a much lesser combat investment still be able to put paid to serious opponents like the action hero they're trying to be? It's easy to make it feel like an MMORPG, where all the canned dialogue talks about what a great hero you are but you're still just fighting level-adjusted palette swaps of wolves the whole way through.<br /> <br /> You're absolutely right that the outcome is kind of unsatisfactory. However, I'm not sure how to untie that knot without just giving up and running a Dragon-Blooded game. If you look at the stories Dawns like that are based on, they're stories about characters who often seem to be in danger, dancing on the knife's edge between life and death, but <i>always win anyway. </i>You can't do that in a game -- if the mechanics say &quot;by the way, this character always wins&quot; then that's right there and it's nearly impossible to ignore it and pretend they're in trouble, but if the mechanics actually put the character in serious peril all the time, they're going to lose a lot, which feels wrong. The closest you can get to reproducing that narrative structure with actual game mechanics is something like FATE's lose-to-win mechanic, which doesn't capture the feel of it at all and makes the apparent tension of conflict seem like a sort of highly ritualized symbolic theatre performance that I think would not satisfy people who come to the table to play Kenshin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-05-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:02:52-07:00","id":859949,"title":"","content":"If the fight is going to be trivial, don't roll it, just RP it. A group of Solars should be hard to challenge in direct combat.<br /> <br /> Use a small BG of elite bodyguards to defend other the main guy. It will suck away the attacker Initiative, because if they decide to attack the bodyguards, they will only get back 1 initiative and with the defense pool for Elite BG a good boss should be able to withstand the attack otherwise.<br /> Spice it up with a ranged BG that will suck away PCs initiative even more and make them think about the dangers of crashing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Elder exalted should never be QC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:18:41-07:00","id":859958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859949#post859949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the fight is going to be trivial, don't roll it, just RP it. A group of Solars should be hard to challenge in direct combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets really dissatisfying when easily more than 20% of Charms (possibly closer to 25%) and a good 1/3 of the system is dedicated to crunch-heavy fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:19:38-07:00","id":859959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859949#post859949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Elder exalted should never be QC.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a noble ideal, but I'm not doing a full, game-legal sheet with 30 interlocking charmpicks, possibly for charms that haven't been written officially yet, for some guy whose main purpose in the story is to fight the party, and who is probably going to die within four rounds if he fights the party. Exalted is a high-prep game and you have to make tradeoffs; I have no doubt that if 3e ever publishes stats for Ligier, he will be a QC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:19:31-07:00","id":859984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859938#post859938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the flipside, having 9 out of every 10 fights just total curb stomps that really aren't worth taking the time to play out because the outcome is painfully obvious, is fucking boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just gonna say it: if your players don't want most combat to be a boring foregone conclusion, then they shouldn't have made characters that render 99% of opponents trivial. It is reasonable to expect the system to be robust enough to accommodate Solar combat ability, but it's not reasonable to expect that same system to operate uniformly at all levels. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11216_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11216\" data-vbnamecard=\"11216\">Grindavikur</a> is describing really <i>is </i>an outlier situation: a full party of combat-optimized Solars with two Dawn Castes and complementary, overlapping competencies, run by players who are clearly making a concerted effort to apply maximum force to every situation. Under those circumstances, what <i>should </i>happen, exactly? Seriously. <i>What is the expected outcome of this scenario?</i><br /> <br /> The game tells us - almost all enemies die messy, futile deaths, with the exception of those few who are so powerful and dangerous that they can challenge a warband of Solar Exalted. And isn't that what the players want? What they have decided they want, by making such characters in the first place and playing them in such a fashion? In fact I'm gonna go one step further and suggest that if this <i>wasn't </i>the result someone would cry foul. &quot;My friends and I made the most terrifying combat Solar group the rules would allow us to make, but we still struggle to win sometimes against enemies that aren't as extreme as we are. What gives?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not knocking the group. Really. I'm not saying &quot;Y'all are playing wrong, lemme show you how to do it the right way.&quot; What I am saying is this: <i>If </i>the players are still having fun, <i>then </i>there is no problem. But <i>if </i>the players are not having fun because the game seems too easy, <i>then </i>maybe the focus should be less on trying to put the game system into a chokehold and more on creating characters that will be satisfying participants in the stories being told. I don't know if there is a mismatch here or not, but it sounds like there could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:33:40-07:00","id":859991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859908#post859908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while I don't have a problem with my players succeeding when they lay out plans, follow them, deal with complications and wrinkles, and finish things without anyone but dead enemies having seen them exercise supernatural skill. My problem is that I'm having such a hard time plotting out more than a few TYPES of difficult combats...<br /> <br /> Again, I can write out combatants who can challenge these characters. It's not a matter of me not knowing how to write an intelligent villain, or a threatening combatant, it's justifying it all the time, and justifying them being strong against what the players are good at every time...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an important point that I'd like to draw attention to: if the only statted person you can use that will challenge the Dawn Caste is Octavian, how many times can you justify him showing up in a story?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not even sure that a full Wyld hunt <i>would</i> be a problem for my Dawn, now that he has Bulwark Stance. The same goes for the QC Lunars, Sidereal, every god except Ahlat, every elemental except Fakharu, and every animal in the book including the Tyrant Lizard. And I can't have a prince of Hell or a Directon's elemental censure come up every single game, but that's about the power tier I need to include to keep my Dawn on his toes. And we're only Essence 1! With barely twenty charms each! I shouldn't have to work so hard to dredge up something of merit for the party to engage every session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859908#post859908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might try in the future to force wedges in that split the party more often, so they can't cover each others weaknesses/the thrown character with high awareness can't prevent ambushes/etc, but I'll need to be careful so it doesn't make them decide to just get glued together at the hip.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I have ruled in my game, which all my players loved and which definitely helps with this problem, is that anyone can negate an <i>ambush</i> (which negates your Defense and gives the attackers a free combat round) by succeeding at an Awareness check, and if they use a free action to warn the party the party reduces that ambush to a <i>surprise attack</i> (-2 Defense and no free combat round), but only by beating the Awareness check themselves can they completely protect themselves from the deleterious effects of a good ambush. This has gone over quite well, and I would highly recommend adopting it as a house rule to Storytellers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859913#post859913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't have every antagonist be capable of threatening a Solar circle because pretty much nothing <i>is</i> capable of threatening a Solar circle. Big dramatic showdowns that can threaten the lives of a Dawn and their Solar buddies should be very rare, climactic events, not a regular occurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are degrees of rarity. &quot;Rare&quot; in the sense of &quot;once every month of concerted adventuring which we represent in a single session&quot; is what I want, what I would consider reasonable from a pacing perspective. Rare in the sense of &quot;a battle only seen once an age, only witnessed by a few and recorded in the tomes of legend&quot; is what we <i>have</i> and that is frankly horrible pacing for an episodic weekly campaign.<br /> <br /> Any battle that involves a second circle demon in Creation, or a celestial censor, or an ancient priest of Oblivion, should have <i>massive</i> narrative impact. It's the sort of thing you should be throwing in at the <i>end </i>of a chapter or even chronicle, but what are your players supposed to do in the mean time? If instead you do this once per session you'll give the players the impression that Creation revolves around them and that all lesser threats are beneath their notice, which begins to feel like everybody is Saitama in <i>One Punch Man</i> wandering the Earth casually bulldozing over every villain. It's boring. It makes the villains seem like jokes, even if the rest of the world treats them with fear and awe.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller I try to make every session fun and challenging. There are no sessions where nothing happens, there are no sessions where the players are completely safe. And I try to build tension over a chronicle, with smaller fights leading to bigger fights and that rising tension eventually becomes a boss battle with something like a directional god of war. But I can't do <i>both</i> of those things if the war god is the only toy in my toy box that actually <i>will</i> challenge the party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859945#post859945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game could definitely use more elder Exalted QCs with heft, but on the whole, I'm a little skeptical that the answer is to buff the antagonists. A lot of the disparity seems to be the result of how obscenely strong a devoted combat-supernal character can get, but a mid-range combatant with 4-6 dice in their combat pools and two combat charms is supposed to be fun to play in a fight, so if you make it so the former type of character is routinely given a tough time, the latter is going to get slaughtered without a constant tanking escort, and then the game veers toward everyone taking extremely combat-focused builds because they &quot;have&quot; to, which annoys the people who didn't want to build that way, and annoys the actual combat monkeys because they're too similar to everybody else.<br /> <br /> I think this is a more structural flaw with the way the game is than perhaps people are giving it credit for. A Solar already starts out as among the best of the best in the thing they're good at, which has the perverse effect of reducing its ability to be an engaging challenge for them. The problem you are running into isn't actually any worse than what happens if you try to run a mystery for a heavily-invested Investigation Supernal character, or naval obstacles at a heavily-invested Sail Supernal character, or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier on, you really <i>have</i> to tailor each challenge to each player in Exalted. The same combat can't be both hard and satisfying for both the Dawn and the Eclipse. It's just not possible in a system that so heavily favors specialization and focus. One of the first games we did at Solar tier was telling on this point: a large battlegroup of Great Cats attacked the party, and within one round every character who wasn't within the Dawn's defend other range was defeated, and everyone inside that range took no damage over four rounds while he steadily decimated their entire army.<br /> <br /> When I plan games now I try to include at least one story-worthy element for each character to show off in. For example, our current combat involves a war band of forest spirits attacking a Dynast town and includes a little something for everyone: for the Dawn I wrote up the above Lunar, the Twilight Crafter is busy combat-repairing the town's broken wall, the Zenith war leader is keeping the Treant army at bay, the Night is engaged in an <i>Enemy at the Gates</i> sniper fight with the trickster Lunar that started this whole mess, and the Eclipse will most likely storm the Dynast garrison and compel them to stop cowering like frightened children and actually do some of that stewarding they always brag about.<br /> <br /> It is <i>much</i> easier to make five separate challenges that please each character than one challenge that pleases them all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859945#post859945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're absolutely right that the outcome is kind of unsatisfactory. However, I'm not sure how to untie that knot without just giving up and running a Dragon-Blooded game. If you look at the stories Dawns like that are based on, they're stories about characters who often seem to be in danger, dancing on the knife's edge between life and death, but <i>always win anyway. </i>You can't do that in a game -- if the mechanics say &quot;by the way, this character always wins&quot; then that's right there and it's nearly impossible to ignore it and pretend they're in trouble, but if the mechanics actually put the character in serious peril all the time, they're going to lose a lot, which feels wrong. The closest you can get to reproducing that narrative structure with actual game mechanics is something like FATE's lose-to-win mechanic, which doesn't capture the feel of it at all and makes the apparent tension of conflict seem like a sort of highly ritualized symbolic theatre performance that I think would not satisfy people who come to the table to play Kenshin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best solution to what you are describing is to have there be a varied tier of powers in the setting, most of which the heroes can bulldoze right over and many of which they cannot. In the <i>Ramayana</i> for example, there is this segment where the &quot;villain&quot; Ravana goes on a massive power trip and duels all the great powers of the world one after another, starting with the gods in heaven, working his way down to the demons of Hell and hitting most everything in between. He trounces all those guys with style, but at one point Death itself threatens to kick his ass and is only stopped by the lord of the Underworld, who doesn't want Ravana to be his problem. Ravana also has a long-running feud with the manifestation of Time, who openly mocks his attempts at relevancy. So even in this upper-limit power tier that Ravana occupies he still has things that can humble him and that is important because it makes him seem relatable and human.<br /> <br /> Ex2 struck something like a balance there. Yeah, your starting circle had perfects and that meant that about 80% of the setting had no chance against them in a straight fight, but there was still more than enough out there to justify a seriously difficult fight during every week's session. The problem I'm running into in Ex3 is that with only the antagonists in the backer PDF the upper limit on power is the <i>only</i> bracket that does this, and no one in this upper echelon has the time or wherewithal to mess with the starting Solars once a week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859949#post859949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the fight is going to be trivial, don't roll it, just RP it. A group of Solars should be hard to challenge in direct combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I'm running into is that unless your fight involves the four toughest things currently statted in the setting, you <i>would</i> just roll one simplified combat roll or RP the results for a focused Dawn caste. Full Wyld hunt with elder Immaculates? One roll. Full squadron of Brides of Ahlat? One roll. A freakin' T-Rex with unlocked magic abilities? One roll. Would you enjoy playing 12+ sessions of a game where every fight was won so cheaply? Because my patience for such a system would wear thin very quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859949#post859949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Elder exalted should never be QC.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> While I am somewhat... displeased by their implementation, I think QC is just how Onyx Path is writing out antagonists now. It really has nothing to do with power tier and everything to do with ease of use and saving spread space, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-05-2016, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:39:21-07:00","id":859997,"title":"","content":"Well, to provide a more fair writeup<br /> <br /> We have one Supernal Thrown Dawn, with investment in Athletics, Awareness, and Stealth<br /> We have one Supernal Melee Dawn, with investment in Investigation and Athletics<br /> We have one Supernal Presence Zenith, with very, very mild investment in Archery and Ride (A single charm in Ride, 2 in Archery)<br /> We have one Supernal Occult Twilight, who has two charms in Righteous Devil Style, and an Ox Body<br /> <br /> 99% of my headaches in combat come from the Dawns covering each other and their two squishier circle mates very well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859984#post859984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not knocking the group. Really. I'm not saying &quot;Y'all are playing wrong, lemme show you how to do it the right way.&quot; What I am saying is this: <i>If </i>the players are still having fun, <i>then </i>there is no problem. But <i>if </i>the players are not having fun because the game seems too easy, <i>then </i>maybe the focus should be less on trying to put the game system into a chokehold and more on creating characters that will be satisfying participants in the stories being told. I don't know if there is a mismatch here or not, but it sounds like there could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>My paranoid worry is that after too long of combat being way too easy for the players who've taken a lot of time and energy to put together good combat suites and learn the combat system top to bottom, is that it will become boring and unfun for them in the future. Right NOW they think it's fun. I'm trying to plot for when curbstomps stop being fun.<br /> <br /> Second Edit: And funnily enough it'll probably be EASIER to write challenging combats when they're E4 and E5 than right now. By then they'll probably have dropped all pretense of pretending to be mortals in public, moved on to challenges like trying to noogie Deathlords bald and restructure Heaven, and I'll have no excuses required to say &quot;Ah hello here is a Third Circle Demon who has been summoned by one of your angry rivals backed up by said angry Rival and a few sorcerous supermonsters he's stitched and weaved together&quot; or combat threats of similar supernatural might","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","user":"Grindavikur","date":". 04-05-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:50:31-07:00","id":860004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859991#post859991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I have ruled in my game, which all my players loved and which definitely helps with this problem, is that anyone can negate an <i>ambush</i> (which negates your Defense and gives the attackers a free combat round) by succeeding at an Awareness check, and if they use a free action to warn the party the party reduces that ambush to a <i>surprise attack</i> (-2 Defense and no free combat round), but only by beating the Awareness check themselves can they completely protect themselves from the deleterious effects of a good ambush. This has gone over quite well, and I would highly recommend adopting it as a house rule to Storytellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is even a houserule.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li> Attacker hides.</li> <li> Party approaches, they get to roll Awareness to spot the attacker.</li> <li> If any of them is successful, they can cry out and start JB.</li> <li> The attacker gets to ambush only those characters that failed to spot him and failed the JB roll (are after him in the initiative ladder).</li> <li> Characters that failed the spot check, but placed before the attacker initiative are treating it as surprise attack.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:59:52-07:00","id":860009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859997#post859997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to provide a more fair writeup<br /> <br /> We have one Supernal Thrown Dawn, with investment in Athletics, Awareness, and Stealth<br /> We have one Supernal Melee Dawn, with investment in Investigation and Athletics<br /> We have one Supernal Presence Zenith, with very, very mild investment in Archery and Ride (A single charm in Ride, 2 in Archery)<br /> We have one Supernal Occult Twilight, who has two charms in Righteous Devil Style, and an Ox Body<br /> <br /> 99% of my headaches in combat come from the Dawns covering each other and their two squishier circle mates very well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My paranoid worry is that after too long of combat being way too easy for the players who've taken a lot of time and energy to put together good combat suites and learn the combat system top to bottom, is that it will become boring and unfun for them in the future. Right NOW they think it's fun. I'm trying to plot for when curbstomps stop being fun.<br /> <br /> Second Edit: And funnily enough it'll probably be EASIER to write challenging combats when they're E4 and E5 than right now. By then they'll probably have dropped all pretense of pretending to be mortals in public, moved on to challenges like trying to noogie Deathlords bald and restructure Heaven, and I'll have no excuses required to say &quot;Ah hello here is a Third Circle Demon who has been summoned by one of your angry rivals backed up by said angry Rival and a few sorcerous supermonsters he's stitched and weaved together&quot; or combat threats of similar supernatural might</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, your characters do not exist in a vacuum. Get a group of Essence 3-4 gods, each with an exalted character, or a school of enlightened/ wyld enhanced/ shamanic / MA guys that are the powers in the area that finally noticed them. Or the Bull of the North with his tiger warriors armed artifact weapons. Or 7 Fae warriors just looking for a fight/essence. You can only be hidden for so long without triggering something, say from a guild caravan, or a God that has connections or a group of sidereal/Lunars hunting for a full circle of solars. Remember, they are the equivalent of low yield nukes, not just field artillery. Respond accordingly to the threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:11:40-07:00","id":860013,"title":"","content":"Seems to me that that might be worse for the &quot;realism&quot; of the setting than letting them go unnoticed a while longer.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if your players are okay with stomping everyone for the time being, why not just tell the players that if they want harder fights they should go out and pick them? Once easy wins gets stale, I doubt they'll have much trouble increasing their ambitions and decreasing their discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:47:47-07:00","id":860031,"title":"","content":"I also have a few problems with designing good encounters for my group. We have a Supernal Archery, Brawl and Stealth with everybody having invested mostly in combat charms. Everybody except the Supernal Brawl is very well rounded and on a power level I expected from Essence 1 Solars with Supernals.<br /> The Brawl is on a whole different level though. He can pretty much one hit ko everything from 1 Initiative (Increasing Strength Exercise, Hammer on Iron Technique, Fivefold Fury Onslaught or if he doesn't feel like it he &quot;just&quot; uses Heaven Thunder Hammer and Thunderbolt Attack Prana after he build up a bit of Ini). If I would design an encounter around the power level of the dawn the other two would be dead in one hit. While it is our first 3rd Edition campaign and all three characters are not optimized the power gap seems to be extrem. <br /> <br /> The other two are no problem at all. They wanted to be good at other things than punching things so I can challenge them without much problems. I'm also on the side that not every single fight against some random animals or bandits should be a something that strikes fear into the players hearts. Those encounters are probably better off just being RP'ed out. Or not being fought at all. The players are Solars and they should feel powerful...<br /> <br /> Another concern I have as a player in my first 3E round is a result of a similar constellation. We have Zenith with Supernal Survival and a boosted beyond everything godblooded Snow Lion, and a (again) Supernal Brawl Dawn specializing on grapples (I'm I the only one thinking grapples are one of the most if not the most dangerous weapon out there?) and I think War. Meanwhile I'm planning on playing a Supernal Craft Twilight. <br /> In 2e I made the experience that it is EXTREMELY frustrating to play a non-combat character in a combat oriented group (it was a master physician and crafter with almost every single medicine charm... Only three of those were used more than 3 times in a whole year of play). I won't make that mistake ever again. <br /> So my Supernal Crafter got a nice pair of Wings and the Silver Voiced Nightingale Charms up to the form, one dodge charm and a Ox-Body Technique. I certainly know that the power gap between this build and the Supernal Brawl is gonna be freaking huge. No way around that, and that is okay. But I can't see my ST creating engaging combat encounters in this constellation. As soon as it gets challenging for the Dawn my character is gonna die from being looked at. At least that is what it feels like, even though I tried to round out the character with combat charms which resulted in me not beeing able to build the stuff I wanted to build from the very beginning. Already very frustrating I must admitt. <br /> I don't have much experience with Solar Melee (the Supernal Sneak only has around 3 charms) or Thrown so I can't say much about the charm trees, but Brawl looks incredible strong. Strong enough to hurt the game with the power gap. <br /> <br /> I really think that every player and the ST need to agree beforehand to how much combat investment the characters are going to have. Everyone should be on a at least somewhat comparable level. Else it is going to be extremely difficult to make challenging combat encounters that can engage the whole group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:50:17-07:00","id":860033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859991#post859991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are degrees of rarity. &quot;Rare&quot; in the sense of &quot;once every month of concerted adventuring which we represent in a single session&quot; is what I want, what I would consider reasonable from a pacing perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...wait, you want to have an opponent show up once per session (meaning approximately once per month of in-game time) that is capable of challenging a pair of Dawn Caste murder-machines in a stand up fight? I can see why you are having issues. This isn't a problem with the system, it's a problem with <i>expectations</i>. Both yours, and those of your players.<br /> <br /> Let's recalibrate for a moment. Set combat aside for now. Let's say instead of combat, I have a player whose character strives to be the fastest man in Creation. He loves footraces. <i>Loves </i>them. He lives to test himself against the fastest runners across the world. So of course, he goes heavy into Athletics, right? That makes sense! Supernal Athletics and all the relevant Charms. Then this exchange happens:<br /> <br /> <b>ST: </b>You reach a new town. It's bigger than the last few, so there are several thousand people here. That makes it the biggest town for days in any direction.<br /> <b>Player: </b>Sweet! I challenge the local youths to a footrace. Surely there is someone here worthy of competition!<br /> <b>ST: </b>...sure. Okay, they're game. You guys run the race the day after next. Uh...do you want to roll it out?<br /> <b>Player: </b>Of course!<br /> <b>ST: </b>Okay, go for it. Extended Athletics roll, difficulty, ah...2 for the uneven ground, terminus five. First one to 20 successes wins.<br /> <b>Player: </b>This is my <i>jam, </i>baby!<br /> *dice rolls*<br /> <b>Player: </b>Aww yeah, 23 successes!<br /> <b>ST: </b>The fastest youth rolled three. You win. Everyone is awed. Uh, what is everyone else up to in the meantime?<br /> <b>Player: </b>Wait! Er...anybody want a rematch?<br /> <b>ST: </b>They do not.<br /> <b>Player: </b>Oh. Um...okay.<br /> <b>ST: </b>Are you <i>pouting?</i><br /> <b>Player: </b>...no.<br /> <br /> So what's wrong with this scenario? I'm sure you can guess. The player obviously likes the idea of his character being defined by &quot;the race&quot; but made the mistake of making himself so good that he has no competition (or at least very, very little - the kind that won't come up every session, or even every story). He's like the dog who chases the car and doesn't have any idea what to do with it once he catches it, except that he's a Solar and he can come out of character creation <i>having already caught the car</i>.<br /> <br /> This is actually a problem that has been investigated in dramatic media before - the warrior so skilled that he wanders the world searching for someone who can challenge him, but who is perpetually disappointed. Oh, the drama! Oh, the angst! It's a tempting idea to base a character around, except that it overlooks one crucial thing: these characters are goddamned <i>miserable</i> because the lack of challenge has sapped them of any ability to enjoy the thing they are best at, and to which they have devoted their lives. They are <i>bored</i>. So guess what happens to a player who makes a character like this?<br /> <br /> Exalted lets players make Solars, and then it sets the ceiling for what they can accomplish very, very high. Players are often conditioned to reach as high as they can by other games, because not doing so results in you being unhappy when you struggle to have an impact on the game. Exalted introduces the potential for the corresponding, opposite problem: you can start so powerful in a given area of competence that you can only be challenged by a very select few, who will come along very rarely. Before you reach so high, it behooves you to ask: <i>do I want this</i><i>? </i>If the answer is no - if it's not the trophy but the race that you find interesting - then maybe you shouldn't. At least, not right away.<br /> <br /> Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:52:24-07:00","id":860034,"title":"","content":"Creating challenging enemies for brawl users doesn't mean giving them lots of damage and creating a rocket tag situation, it means using multiple enemies against whom a Fivefold Fury Onslaught or Crashing Wave Throw would be overkill, or using really tough enemies who can survive those kinds of attacks. Neither of those options would create a situation where the other PCs are going to die before they can contribute to the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T19:10:27-07:00","id":860044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860031#post860031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a few problems with designing good encounters for my group. We have a Supernal Archery, Brawl and Stealth with everybody having invested mostly in combat charms. Everybody except the Supernal Brawl is very well rounded and on a power level I expected from Essence 1 Solars with Supernals.<br /> The Brawl is on a whole different level though. He can pretty much one hit ko everything from 1 Initiative (Increasing Strength Exercise, Hammer on Iron Technique, Fivefold Fury Onslaught or if he doesn't feel like it he &quot;just&quot; uses Heaven Thunder Hammer and Thunderbolt Attack Prana after he build up a bit of Ini). If I would design an encounter around the power level of the dawn the other two would be dead in one hit. While it is our first 3rd Edition campaign and all three characters are not optimized the power gap seems to be extrem.<br /> <br /> The other two are no problem at all. They wanted to be good at other things than punching things so I can challenge them without much problems. I'm also on the side that not every single fight against some random animals or bandits should be a something that strikes fear into the players hearts. Those encounters are probably better off just being RP'ed out. Or not being fought at all. The players are Solars and they should feel powerful...<br /> <br /> Another concern I have as a player in my first 3E round is a result of a similar constellation. We have Zenith with Supernal Survival and a boosted beyond everything godblooded Snow Lion, and a (again) Supernal Brawl Dawn specializing on grapples (I'm I the only one thinking grapples are one of the most if not the most dangerous weapon out there?) and I think War. Meanwhile I'm planning on playing a Supernal Craft Twilight.<br /> In 2e I made the experience that it is EXTREMELY frustrating to play a non-combat character in a combat oriented group (it was a master physician and crafter with almost every single medicine charm... Only three of those were used more than 3 times in a whole year of play). I won't make that mistake ever again.<br /> So my Supernal Crafter got a nice pair of Wings and the Silver Voiced Nightingale Charms up to the form, one dodge charm and a Ox-Body Technique. I certainly know that the power gap between this build and the Supernal Brawl is gonna be freaking huge. No way around that, and that is okay. But I can't see my ST creating engaging combat encounters in this constellation. As soon as it gets challenging for the Dawn my character is gonna die from being looked at. At least that is what it feels like, even though I tried to round out the character with combat charms which resulted in me not beeing able to build the stuff I wanted to build from the very beginning. Already very frustrating I must admitt.<br /> I don't have much experience with Solar Melee (the Supernal Sneak only has around 3 charms) or Thrown so I can't say much about the charm trees, but Brawl looks incredible strong. Strong enough to hurt the game with the power gap.<br /> <br /> I really think that every player and the ST need to agree beforehand to how much combat investment the characters are going to have. Everyone should be on a at least somewhat comparable level. Else it is going to be extremely difficult to make challenging combat encounters that can engage the whole group.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does your dawns keep being hammered when they reset after he does his decisive? if he is Essence 1, then he resets to 4. That means that he is a lucky hit away from crash. Also, if they are battling battle group, they only get 1 initiate a hit, no matter how much damage. I would also discount a grapple vs Legendary size or battle group, just because of how many he can affect with a grapple. Also look at the fair folk cataphract, thrown 5 of those plus an Ess 4 leader with better charms, plus about 40-100 goblins and see what happens. Give them all griffins or manticores as mounts, with the leader having the ability to use Invisbility or illusion to hide what they all are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T19:20:03-07:00","id":860049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=859984#post859984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I am saying is this: <i>If </i>the players are still having fun, <i>then </i>there is no problem. But <i>if </i>the players are not having fun because the game seems too easy, <i>then </i>maybe the focus should be less on trying to put the game system into a chokehold and more on creating characters that will be satisfying participants in the stories being told. I don't know if there is a mismatch here or not, but it sounds like there could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we should be limiting player choice if other avenues exist to address an in-game problem. Certainly, we could very easily make the system more competitive by removing Supernal skills from play, but that's less fun and expressive for the players.<br /> <br /> The sort of things I would do to bump up the general difficulty of the antagonists would be quite minor and easy to implement for the most part; just adding +4 soak and a couple extra health levels to most things would help tremendously. Assume that most exalts will be at least as competent as your Solars in their fields of expertise, meaning 5s instead of 3s and 4s in their relevant skills and attributes. If you want to take an antagonist and make it a boss fight, give it other ways to generate initiative or stay out of crash (Legendary Size is a solid choice) and something that allows it to attack twice a turn in certain situations. That's about it, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T19:46:41-07:00","id":860061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860033#post860033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...wait, you want to have an opponent show up once per session (meaning approximately once per month of in-game time) that is capable of challenging a pair of Dawn Caste murder-machines in a stand up fight? I can see why you are having issues. This isn't a problem with the system, it's a problem with <i>expectations</i>. Both yours, and those of your players.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost surreal in terms of how true to our experiences it has been so far. I don't think I could have put it better.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860033#post860033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted lets players make Solars, and then it sets the ceiling for what they can accomplish very, very high. Players are often conditioned to reach as high as they can by other games, because not doing so results in you being unhappy when you struggle to have an impact on the game. Exalted introduces the potential for the corresponding, opposite problem: you can start so powerful in a given area of competence that you can only be challenged by a very select few, who will come along very rarely. Before you reach so high, it behooves you to ask: <i>do I want this</i><i>? </i>If the answer is no - if it's not the trophy but the race that you find interesting - then maybe you shouldn't. At least, not right away.<br /> <br /> This is actually a problem that has been investigated in dramatic media before - the warrior so skilled that he wanders the world searching for someone who can challenge him, but who is perpetually disappointed. Oh, the drama! Oh, the angst! It's a tempting idea to base a character around, except that it overlooks one crucial thing: these characters are goddamned <i>miserable</i> because the lack of challenge has sapped them of any ability to enjoy the thing they are best at, and to which they have devoted their lives. They are <i>bored</i>. So guess what happens to a player who makes a character like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting because I can see that we are having very similar experience at our tables, or at least that you perfectly understand the problem I am having, but obviously we've come to very different conclusions.<br /> <br /> Again, you can absolutely address this problem by limiting player options or suggesting that players do so themselves. What I would argue is that this creates a less interesting, dynamic and mythical setting. It becomes a game where most players are going to be encountering themes of disappointment instead of wonder and triumph, which is what I think most of the game should be reaching for. The former is certainly a valid story idea, but I'd rather that this be a niche experience that STs and players agree on rather than a situation endemic to the system and setting itself. In the example you gave above I'd let the Solar thoroughly shame the village youths, who then spread word of his excellence to the nearby mountain god, who in turn tells the Hare-totem Lunar that he's heard of someone who puts even their speed to shame, and what ensues is a legitimately challenging contest of skill because I love how pulpy and epic Exalted is.<br /> <br /> The problem being, of course, that this Hare Lunar would fare little better than the village youths at present. In order to find a real challenge he'd have to bribe a sorcerer to summon a second circle soul of Adorjan or something, which is going wayyyy further out on a limb than even I like to do in my epic stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:41:34-07:00","id":860116,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it matters, but I do think that the heights of what is available to a PC from character creation <i>can </i>present some serious challenges that are not easily resolved. One of my players in a game I will be STing has made a Twilight with Supernal Investigation and taken Charms up to <i>Irresistible Questioning Technique</i>. He also has a mentor/adversary in the form of an imprisoned second circle demon, from whom he wrested the secrets of Sorcery. The demon in question is a scheming, homicidal genius who <i>clearly </i>needs to be the Hannibal to my player's Clarice Starling. It's a great story hook! Buuut...<br /> <br /> I have lost <i>far less </i>sleep concerned with whether he can challenge the party in combat than I have wrestling with how the <i>hell </i>to let him actually be that scheming nemesis, when my player can just mark off some motes and Willpower and force my villain to spill the beans whenever he wants to. I have a few ideas. But it's hard! The wiggle room allowed by <i>IQT</i> is razor-thin, and I can't just make him immune to it without devaluing the investment my player made. I could just throw my hands up and say, &quot;Welp, you win! That Charm is bonkers and I got nothing. Here's his devious plan.&quot; But that undermines the whole point - the player gave me this villain because he wants to have his Moriarty! How to both let the PC be the brilliant detective he is while still giving him a nemesis he can't unravel with trivial ease? This is the kind of problem that is easy to miss as a player but drives an ST nuts. Beyond that, it threatens to make a major part of the character moot in the future, too - what's the point of playing a brilliant detective when you can just make anybody confess right away? <u>The Maltese Falcon</u> would be a much shorter novel if Sam Spade knew Investigation Charms.<br /> <br /> So a warning to players! If you like robbing houses, a skeleton key is a great investment. But if you <i>like </i><i>picking locks</i>, it's a terrible one. In that case, make a character who has a reason to need lockpicks instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:27:12-07:00","id":860129,"title":"","content":"While your specific charm example matters a lot less than your overall point (Which I agree with), my players proposed an easy set of solutions for that problem, ranging from just giving minions incomplete/false knowledge, to &quot;Hold on, IQT says they answer truthfully and to their fullest knowledge, but doesn't specify how. They could answer in riddles or ciphers, code, or even languages the character doesn't speak/slang they have no knowledge of&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T00:10:12-07:00","id":860155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860116#post860116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it matters, but I do think that the heights of what is available to a PC from character creation <i>can </i>present some serious challenges that are not easily resolved. One of my players in a game I will be STing has made a Twilight with Supernal Investigation and taken Charms up to <i>Irresistible Questioning Technique</i>. He also has a mentor/adversary in the form of an imprisoned second circle demon, from whom he wrested the secrets of Sorcery. The demon in question is a scheming, homicidal genius who <i>clearly </i>needs to be the Hannibal to my player's Clarice Starling. It's a great story hook! Buuut...<br /> <br /> I have lost <i>far less </i>sleep concerned with whether he can challenge the party in combat than I have wrestling with how the <i>hell </i>to let him actually be that scheming nemesis, when my player can just mark off some motes and Willpower and force my villain to spill the beans whenever he wants to. I have a few ideas. But it's hard! The wiggle room allowed by <i>IQT</i> is razor-thin, and I can't just make him immune to it without devaluing the investment my player made. I could just throw my hands up and say, &quot;Welp, you win! That Charm is bonkers and I got nothing. Here's his devious plan.&quot; But that undermines the whole point - the player gave me this villain because he wants to have his Moriarty! How to both let the PC be the brilliant detective he is while still giving him a nemesis he can't unravel with trivial ease? This is the kind of problem that is easy to miss as a player but drives an ST nuts. Beyond that, it threatens to make a major part of the character moot in the future, too - what's the point of playing a brilliant detective when you can just make anybody confess right away? <u>The Maltese Falcon</u> would be a much shorter novel if Sam Spade knew Investigation Charms.<br /> <br /> So a warning to players! If you like robbing houses, a skeleton key is a great investment. But if you <i>like </i><i>picking locks</i>, it's a terrible one. In that case, make a character who has a reason to need lockpicks instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have to admit, it's hard not to agree when I see this problem getting directly in the way of a <i>great</i> story hook like that. Mechanics that get in the way of story ideas will never fail to frustrate me. If you would like specific suggestions on how to manage this story hook I'd be happy to help, since it's well within the stated intent of this thread (again, not every challenge need by combat, it's just the one I find most pressing in my game presently). I'm sure there are ways even with <i>IQT</i> that this could be done, as Grindavikur has suggested a few already. The first and most obvious to me is to distract the player with an unrelated crime or riddle while conducting their own plot. Players are always easy to distract, and for some reason they never seem to see the B plot coming until it's too late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860031#post860031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a few problems with designing good encounters for my group. We have a Supernal Archery, Brawl and Stealth with everybody having invested mostly in combat charms. Everybody except the Supernal Brawl is very well rounded and on a power level I expected from Essence 1 Solars with Supernals.<br /> <br /> The Brawl is on a whole different level though. He can pretty much one hit ko everything from 1 Initiative (Increasing Strength Exercise, Hammer on Iron Technique, Fivefold Fury Onslaught or if he doesn't feel like it he &quot;just&quot; uses Heaven Thunder Hammer and Thunderbolt Attack Prana after he build up a bit of Ini). If I would design an encounter around the power level of the dawn the other two would be dead in one hit. While it is our first 3rd Edition campaign and all three characters are not optimized the power gap seems to be extreme.<br /> <br /> I really think that every player and the ST need to agree beforehand to how much combat investment the characters are going to have. Everyone should be on a at least somewhat comparable level. Else it is going to be extremely difficult to make challenging combat encounters that can engage the whole group.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the sound of it, you need to start making custom opponents for this Brawl supernal Solar. If the power gap is really that extreme then you won't be able to make one thing that can challenge all three of these fighters, but making one boss for the Brawler and two lieutenants for the Archery and Stealth Solars would probably work much better. If the <i>characters</i> are aware of this power imbalance they may even break the fights up this way themselves, to improve the odds of success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860031#post860031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another concern I have as a player in my first 3E round is a result of a similar constellation. We have Zenith with Supernal Survival and a boosted beyond everything godblooded Snow Lion, and a (again) Supernal Brawl Dawn specializing on grapples (I'm I the only one thinking grapples are one of the most if not the most dangerous weapon out there?) and I think War. Meanwhile I'm planning on playing a Supernal Craft Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grapples can indeed be a great equalizer, but they do have a few limitations that you might not have noticed at first (I didn't): for one thing there is no rule saying that you can't keep attacking, even if you are the one &quot;losing&quot; the clinch. And remember, for every attack <i>and</i> every damaging hit you land, your opponent will lose one turn of grapple. You also need to be able to land the Grapple in the first place, which is as hard as a normal decisive attack, and then your opponent can resist you again in that opposed control roll. If you find that your grappler is dominating the field too much, attack him with some lesser villains that take advantage of that -2 defense he is suffering just for being in Grapple.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-06-2016, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:35:07-07:00","id":860247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860044#post860044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does your dawns keep being hammered when they reset after he does his decisive? if he is Essence 1, then he resets to 4. That means that he is a lucky hit away from crash. Also, if they are battling battle group, they only get 1 initiate a hit, no matter how much damage. I would also discount a grapple vs Legendary size or battle group, just because of how many he can affect with a grapple. Also look at the fair folk cataphract, thrown 5 of those plus an Ess 4 leader with better charms, plus about 40-100 goblins and see what happens. Give them all griffins or manticores as mounts, with the leader having the ability to use Invisbility or illusion to hide what they all are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the tipps. He has a few Resistance Charms to buff his soak but that is not as effective as his allies and the other two in the group. The Supernal Sneak pops out behind the enemie if it gets hairy for the dawn. He also has a standard parry of 7 which helps and a defensive oriented human champion at his side that occasionally uses Defend Other on him. <br /> I tried with battlegroups... Though in one encounter that was supposed to be a challenge the big bad got destroyed by the Dawn before the battlegroup could engage him or his team (the group got the jump so the BG needed 2 rounds to close distance). Mobility Charms are strong. <br /> <br /> Also if I use the encounter you proposed it would result in 2 deaths. Everybody but the Dawn would be screaming bloody murder at me. The problem is not challenging the Dawn. The problem is challenging the solar without killing the other two that are nowhere near as strong in a fight. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the sound of it, you need to start making custom opponents for this Brawl supernal Solar. If the power gap is really that extreme then you won't be able to make one thing that can challenge all three of these fighters, but making one boss for the Brawler and two lieutenants for the Archery and Stealth Solars would probably work much better. If the <i>characters</i> are aware of this power imbalance they may even break the fights up this way themselves, to improve the odds of success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was in a way my approach for the last battle that was supposed to be a challenge. The enemy was a group of homebrew monsters with a big bad in the middle of a sea. The boss had sent out most of his troops to search for the circle but they snuck in with the help of the supernal sneak and the help of an elemental. To get to him they still needed to clear out a few outposts of these monsters so they weren't even full on motes. <br /> The Supernal Sneak needed to take care of a monster that was able to call those out to hunt the circle back to the lake. That worked well he did that and had a few close calls since this thing was right in the middle of several other monsters. <br /> The Supernal Archery char stood behind and used the range to her advantage till a monster poped out of the sea right in front of her and crashed her after a successful descisive attack. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile a size 3 battlegroup of mutated flying insects with absurdly high evasion was supposed to be a buffer for the big bad but was mostly ignored till the end. <br /> <br /> The Dawn now sailed on a little boat to the middle of the sea and opened the fight. After the Join Battle (8 Ini for him) he jumped with athletic charms and comboed the hardness 8 boss with 25 HL and the Legendary Size Merit into his last two -2 HL. The next Initiative 9 decisive attack from the Supernal Archery took him to -4. After that the fight was easy. And the Size 3 battlegroup had yet to engage anybody (the players were smart with their position). The boss wasn't even able to show his cool abilities cause of that... I really need to think around the explosive power of the Brawl character. <br /> <br /> In the whole fight was only one thing that could have been described dangerous. There was one 19 Initiative attack because the dawn got withered hard by the boss after he comboed him (and was free falling mid air after that). The dawn casually buffed his parry to 13 so nothing dangerous there. <br /> <br /> That was their &quot;welcome to Essence 2!&quot; fight and the Dawn already announced that he will go even more into combat power... Meanwhile the other two want to do crafting and performance. The power gap is going to get even more extreme. <br /> So yes, I really, really need custome made encounters with special circumstances so the other two can do something else than to just die, while the Dawn can fight a worthy opponent. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grapples can indeed be a great equalizer, but they do have a few limitations that you might not have noticed at first (I didn't): for one thing there is no rule saying that you can't keep attacking, even if you are the one &quot;losing&quot; the clinch. And remember, for every attack <i>and</i> every damaging hit you land, your opponent will lose one turn of grapple. You also need to be able to land the Grapple in the first place, which is as hard as a normal decisive attack, and then your opponent can resist you again in that opposed control roll. If you find that your grappler is dominating the field too much, attack him with some lesser villains that take advantage of that -2 defense he is suffering just for being in Grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily my Dawn does not really care about grapples. He is more the punching type. But all these limitations are only relevant when the Grappler choose to hold the grapple (drag &amp; restrain or savage). The dawn in the group I'm playing in has charms for hitting the grapple so hitting with his normal attack pool is easy. He has Increasing Strength Exercise, so he almost always gets the full + 12 Withering damage from the forfeited controll rolls or + 24 I think with a charm for a few motes (I think it also works with decisive attacks... Alone with Strength Increasing Exercise he gets +7 decisive damage and leaves the enemy prone). He then throws, almost always uses it to cause falling damage (which is absurdly strong this edition) and if he feels like it adds a bit of AoE to it. I need to read up on those charms to undestand how exactly they work. <br /> <br /> Point is: The disadvantages of Grapples aren't that important since you can throw on the same turn you grappled the opponent. As soon as a solar grappler gets the charm to grapple opponents of every size I don't know what to do against that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:58:44-07:00","id":860255,"title":"","content":"The Dawn wants one kind of game and it sounds like the other players want a vey different kind of game. At this point you have an OOC issue and the only way to address it to the satisfaction of all players is OOC. This is beyond the point where you can solve it IC with more challenging fights IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T06:01:13-07:00","id":860257,"title":"","content":"Ryoki, I think you need to stop challenging your Dawn with fair fights. He's a powerhouse, so any NPC who wants to take him down will not fight fair. Focus on range attacks and play keep away if possible. Your Dawn can't hit them if he can't find/reach him. Make the opponent another Solar if you have to get access to the Athletics charms. Solars don't have to be good guys. Abyssals had a really annoying short ranged teleport charm in Ex2, so if you are up to Homebrew you can roll up an Abyssal instead. <br /> <br /> Or be honest with your Dawn. &quot;Dude, this is a new system and the rest of the splat books aren't out yet. I can barely make challenging opponents at your current power level much less when you get more combat charms.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:37:00-07:00","id":860336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860129#post860129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While your specific charm example matters a lot less than your overall point (Which I agree with), my players proposed an easy set of solutions for that problem, ranging from just giving minions incomplete/false knowledge, to &quot;Hold on, IQT says they answer truthfully and to their fullest knowledge, but doesn't specify how. They could answer in riddles or ciphers, code, or even languages the character doesn't speak/slang they have no knowledge of&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great suggestion. In the Vorkosigan series by Lois McMaster Bujold, the main character Miles is not immune to that universe version of truth serum, usually spies are made allergic to it so they die if it is used on them instead of spilling their secrets. Miles did not go through that treatment, but because of the circumstances of his life, his body responds to the serum differently.<br /> He still has to tell truth, but he has total control about how he tells it. So he starts telling the truth, then strays off talking about related topics, that brings memories of some songs so he starts singing, etc.<br /> <br /> On a more practical note how to beat the IQT, how about a chamber with a working on it, that will erase all your memories about your plans once you leave it and when you come back, it will restore them? You can make notes for yourself about what you want to do when you leave the chamber, but IQT will only get those details, without ruining the whole plan.<br /> Why you can even make fake notes for yourself to throw people with IQT off.<br /> <br /> The schema using unrelated crimes for distractions is another great idea. It works even better if your player has Defining/Major intimacy towards solving puzzles and mysteries like that. Even if he knows what his opponent is doing, it should trigger limit rolls.<br /> (I have recently read Mistborn: The Bands of Mourning by Brandon Sanderson where the main villain used exactly this strategy for years to distract the main character.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Use Defend Other on the important NPCs by BG is a good strategy how to help them avoid the grapple. Combine it with ranged attacks by another BG/NPCs and it should become challenging fight for the Dawn.<br /> Sometimes enemies could try to use poison to weaken him. Either on blade or in food/drinks.<br /> <br /> To solve the power discrepancies, you will have to split the group a bit during the combat, giving them different objectives. The Dawn could take care of the main villain and his elites, while the rest of the group takes care of the guards to free the prisoners.<br /> <br /> You will also have to diversify your story if you want to accommodate the social as well as the combat oriented players. The Dawn will feel pretty useless in the Twilights forge or during some treaty negotiation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","user":"Korusef","date":".  Addressing the Dawn thread. 04-06-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:40:28-07:00","id":861214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860247#post860247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the tipps. He has a few Resistance Charms to buff his soak but that is not as effective as his allies and the other two in the group. The Supernal Sneak pops out behind the enemie if it gets hairy for the dawn. He also has a standard parry of 7 which helps and a defensive oriented human champion at his side that occasionally uses Defend Other on him.<br /> I tried with battlegroups... Though in one encounter that was supposed to be a challenge the big bad got destroyed by the Dawn before the battlegroup could engage him or his team (the group got the jump so the BG needed 2 rounds to close distance). Mobility Charms are strong.<br /> <br /> Also if I use the encounter you proposed it would result in 2 deaths. Everybody but the Dawn would be screaming bloody murder at me. The problem is not challenging the Dawn. The problem is challenging the solar without killing the other two that are nowhere near as strong in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that it helps to communicate to my players out of character that there are some fights better left to the specialist, and then making it very very obvious what fights those are. For example, in my last game a bunch of things were attacking this dynast town all at once, but the Terrestrials were holding their own and keeping their cool until they heard the Full Moon Lunar approaching, at which point they simultaneously lost it and started evacuating. My Dawn picked up on that loud and clear, and so did the rest of the party who had plenty of other things to do (never leave someone with nothing to do, they will get bored and try to help) who let him go duel the big bad without much discussion.<br /> <br /> It's only cheating a little bit. Characters will eventually notice a power discrepancy this big, and letting the PCs know about it means they don't have to learn this lesson the hard way.<br /> <br /> As for the Dawn, if you are having trouble competing with him in the one thing he wins at throw other challenges at him. Can he lie or detect lies? Pair him off with a trickster who fools him into beating up his rivals. Make good use of his intimacies. Put him in situations he <i>could</i> punch his way out of but has good reason not to, like having the bad guy be a tyrannical dictator protected by legions of drafted citizen guards who just want to go home and feed their families. Sometimes the best stories in Exalted don't involve dice, just hard character decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T20:57:38-07:00","id":861569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=860116#post860116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that undermines the whole point - the player gave me this villain because he wants to have his Moriarty! How to both let the PC be the brilliant detective he is while still giving him a nemesis he can't unravel with trivial ease? This is the kind of problem that is easy to miss as a player but drives an ST nuts. Beyond that, it threatens to make a major part of the character moot in the future, too - what's the point of playing a brilliant detective when you can just make anybody confess right away? <u>The Maltese Falcon</u> would be a much shorter novel if Sam Spade knew Investigation Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Terrestrial Working to grant a mutation - have the demon grant himself a very fantastical version of multiple personality disorder. The dominant personality is the one the player knows, but the second, subversive personality bubbles up when he's not around, and the dominant personality goes to sleep, leaving blank spots in its recollections but permitting it to answer questions like, &quot;Did you call up a nephwrack to eat my children?&quot; with &quot;No, of course not!&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, when the PC inevitably demands, &quot;Have you done anything to sabotage me,&quot; the proper response is a belly laugh and, &quot;Everything I can think of!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:12:10-07:00","id":861882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=861569#post861569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, when the PC inevitably demands, &quot;Have you done anything to sabotage me,&quot; the proper response is a belly laugh and, &quot;Everything I can think of!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, this is my preferred means of handling the problem. Tell the truth, but perhaps not a truth that is terribly helpful (or better yet, a truth that sends the PC off in the wrong direction). The demon is an arrogant genius, after all, so if he can provoke the PC into asking the wrong questions...<br /> <br /> The problem I have with a lot of the obvious solutions that have already been suggested is that they attempt to subvert the rules by rules-lawyering harder. IMO the job of the ST (in this case, me) is not to &quot;beat&quot; the PC by rendering his Charm selection null. It's to allow that choice to be meaningful and useful without exploding the stories that the player obviously wants to tell. The game is supposed to be fun, after all, and it's rarely fun to discover that your Charms only work as advertised when there's not a lot on the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:19:40-07:00","id":862690,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow the demon to defeat the spirit of Irresistible Questioning Technique, I think. If the player wanted that story <i>and</i> wanted to use Irresitible Questioning Technique on the demon, it seems like the best way to go is just to have the demon be sincere when called for, like &quot;Okay, okay, I admit it: I'm never going to stop attempting to corrupt you and I intend to either make you useful to me or destroy you in the process. Fair cop. On the other hand, you're the one with all the power in this relationship, I can't make you do anything you don't want to, and there are many things you need that I can provide for you, so it sounds like a pretty good deal, right?&quot; In other words, you need to rely on a form of corruption that doesn't fail when it's exposed.<br /> <br /> This is a bit atypical, and it's harder to pull off, but it seems like the only way to be true to the nature of the story and the character -- to make it about the lure of corruption even to someone whose eyes are open, and the dangers of hubris in assuming you're safe. Hannibal didn't actually <i>lie</i> to people very much, and they knew he was a son of a bitch. His power was in insight. So give the demon a bunch of Read Intentions kit, Charisma to go with their Manipulation, and make them good at finding the things that could make becoming a pawn of the Yozis or adopting the demon's worldview appealing to the Solar, and good at pitching those things at opportune moments. In some respects, I think it'd be similar to playing a Shadow in Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-09-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:18:55-07:00","id":863086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=861882#post861882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with a lot of the obvious solutions that have already been suggested is that they attempt to subvert the rules by rules-lawyering harder. IMO the job of the ST (in this case, me) is not to &quot;beat&quot; the PC by rendering his Charm selection null. It's to allow that choice to be meaningful and useful without exploding the stories that the player obviously wants to tell. The game is supposed to be fun, after all, and it's rarely fun to discover that your Charms only work as advertised when there's not a lot on the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't be rendering his choice null - the demon's still got to be honest with anything he knows or does, including things he sees before and after the second personality takes over. It's going to be pretty hard for the demon to deny escaping his confines temporarily, murdering key witnesses, or rerouting the manse's geomancy when he &quot;wakes up&quot; to find himself outside the circle, with blood in his hands, holding a hearthstone, etc.<br /> <br /> If you are describing the demon as the Lecter to the player's Clarice, if he's going to be a subversive, recurring mentor figure whose struggle with the PC is a central part of the PC's story, then he gets to do wacky things to stay in the narrative. He gets this one limited out, and no other NPC does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T06:21:04-07:00","id":863130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=861214#post861214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that it helps to communicate to my players out of character that there are some fights better left to the specialist, and then making it very very obvious what fights those are.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that a fun situation for the other players to be in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:46:45-07:00","id":863167,"title":"","content":"I find the best thing is to have one opponent who is obviously the person for the combat specialist to fight, and then lesser opponents or a battle group for the rest to fight.<br /> Which... sometimes works. Sometimes the PCs don't care and the less skilled ones attack the big boss, but hey, they're perfectly aware of what they're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T20:32:04-07:00","id":863461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=863130#post863130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is that a fun situation for the other players to be in?</div> </div> </div> </div>My players seem to think so. Again, just dont leave anyone with nothing to do. If the crafter, sorcerer, priest and thief all have something to do while the dawn duels the big bad then no one should have a problem. If they do then either you need to make their parts more interesting or if they really just need to fight the big bad every game they should consider making a dawn instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T00:44:54-07:00","id":863517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=863461#post863461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My players seem to think so. Again, just dont leave anyone with nothing to do. If the crafter, sorcerer, priest and thief all have something to do while the dawn duels the big bad then no one should have a problem. If they do then either you need to make their parts more interesting or if they really just need to fight the big bad every game they should consider making a dawn instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot think of any scenario where extra combatants on the party's side (I am referring to players and their retainers) - no matter how relatively combat-lite - would not be able to make a meaningful impact on the battle as a whole. <br /> <br /> My Dawn is pure combat and decks most challenges outright but boy howdy would the tables be turned if he didn't have his faithful Twilight, Zenith and Night around to help (in fact, the one time he didn't he got his arm ripped off).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:59:29-07:00","id":863732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=863517#post863517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot think of any scenario where extra combatants on the party's side (I am referring to players and their retainers) - no matter how relatively combat-lite - would not be able to make a meaningful impact on the battle as a whole. <br /> <br /> My Dawn is pure combat and decks most challenges outright but boy howdy would the tables be turned if he didn't have his faithful Twilight, Zenith and Night around to help (in fact, the one time he didn't he got his arm ripped off).</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games i have found that the risks far outweigh the benefits of this play style. Here is a good way to think of Ex3 combat: every combatant is an Ex2 Abyssal. What i mean by that is that the new system heavily favors the challenger who can deal damage and reap initiative each turn. Without an Ox Body or Resistance charms most characters suffer equally from decisive attacks, but whereas your Dawn will have a high Defense and soak and be able to reliably get initiative each turn, lesser conbatants will struggle to do any damage but will continue to serve as quick and reliable initiative sacks well after they have been put into negatives. In fact, I sent a Terrestrial exalt npc with my Dawn for this most recent showdown, and I fully expect that to be a handicap.<br /> <br /> In Ex2 Ravening Mouth of X meant that the worst thing you could do against an Abyssal was bring a bunch of chaff. The new combat system makes this a serious concern for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T14:32:23-07:00","id":863900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=863732#post863732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my games i have found that the risks far outweigh the benefits of this play style. Here is a good way to think of Ex3 combat: every combatant is an Ex2 Abyssal. What i mean by that is that the new system heavily favors the challenger who can deal damage and reap initiative each turn. Without an Ox Body or Resistance charms most characters suffer equally from decisive attacks, but whereas your Dawn will have a high Defense and soak and be able to reliably get initiative each turn, lesser conbatants will struggle to do any damage but will continue to serve as quick and reliable initiative sacks well after they have been put into negatives. In fact, I sent a Terrestrial exalt npc with my Dawn for this most recent showdown, and I fully expect that to be a handicap.<br /> <br /> In Ex2 Ravening Mouth of X meant that the worst thing you could do against an Abyssal was bring a bunch of chaff. The new combat system makes this a serious concern for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I have not yet found this a problem, for the same reason I have not felt like it was an issue to put mooks with a big bad, neither the players nor he enemy combatants find any traction with dividing their attention (like reaping initiative off a weaker enemy to slap a bigger one)<br /> <br /> The threat of the biggest bad getting a sizable pool of initiative is enough to curb that kind of playing. At my table at least. <br /> <br /> This is the same group that don't feel like they've exercised their right to call themselves exalted if they are not spending at least the 5m drip each turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:28:30-07:00","id":864106,"title":"","content":"I will say, if you're worried about the chaff generating initiative, have the chaff be a battle group, since they only give 1 initiative per hit.<br /> <br /> Saying that, I haven't found that, in combats with 2 or 3 non-bg enemies, this is really a big problem. But then, I never made one enemy far, far tougher (but not stronger) than the other.<br /> If one enemy is all-around better, people will actually attack them to get their initiative down so they can't do killing blows, even if they have better defences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:24:26-07:00","id":864338,"title":"","content":"I should clarify: this is only a problem in Ex3 when you have a HUGE power gap between enemies, like the power gap many are seeing between their focused combat Dawns and everyone else. So my advice here is really only applicable if you have someone head and shoulders above the other antagonists like Ahlat fighting alongside individual Brides. But since I strongly recommend making something <i>that </i>powerful in order to entertain your focused combatant, this shouldnt be all that uncommon an occurance.<br /> <br /> Another consideration is whether or not your combatant has an onslaught negator. Traditionally these are cheap and solars can easily afford to keep one active every turn, but without one pack tactics are still quite effective in Ex3. Basically, I would say that either an onslaught negator or 20+ soak, or both, are what will make the difference between a fight that your whole party can help with and a fight your non-combatants should really let the Dawn handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-13-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T20:47:17-07:00","id":864688,"title":"","content":"Which gives me a fun terrestrial charm concept I might battle-test soon:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Rising Elemental Fury</b></i><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental; Mins: ??? 1 Essence 1;<b> Prerequisites: </b>none; <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial exalt claims the tumult of battle as their own, and commences their onslaught with an eye for capitalizing on the chaos of a coordinated attack. This charm supplements a physical strike, and adds a number of non-charm bonus dice to the attack roll of a withering or decisive attack equal to the target's current Onslaught Penalty. If the target is suffering Onslaught Penalties from another Terrestrial exalt when this charm is invoked, then the user may claim these non-charm bonus dice even if their target is using a charm or effect that allows them to ignore Onslaught Penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T01:34:33-07:00","id":868273,"title":"","content":"So we concluded the War Pig fight last night. If you have forgotten how the first round went here is a refresher:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I built a Full Moon Lunar soak-health beast hoping to create something that would at least last a couple rounds with him. He has better soak than Octavian: 11 from artifact heavy armor, 5 from Stamina, and +4 for his war form, for a total soak of 20 which is what my Dawn has. He has 28 Health levels, 14 of which are -4s. He wields a Dire Lance (Heavy Artifact, Piercing, Reaching) and rolls eleven dice to hit, with +23 raw damage (another +4 for its war form). His Parry is six. He has all Physical attributes and melee/brawl at five. He rides a stat-boosted Hellboar, which is also his totem animal, and gains all of its creature powers in war form. I gave him <i>several</i> of Octavian's powers for good measure but halved their mote cost to account for his smaller mote pool.<br /> <br /> Here is what happened:<br /> <br /> My Dawn got 22 on his join battle roll to my Lunar's 18. My Dawn rides an upgraded Simhatta (son of the Simhatta god) and they both rushed each other and clashed on round one. Both are using the charm Seasoned Beast-Rider's Approach and roll their mounts into combat on their tick. My Lunar gets 18 to hit on the clash but my Dawn rolls 20+, then does 14 withering damage. The Simhatta also wins the clash and does substantial withering damage, but does not crash the Hellboar. The Lunar and Hellboar continue charging past the Dawn, aiming for the nearby town of soft targets. So the Simhatta gives chase and uses a willpower to reflexively attack again with decisive damage, killing the Hellboar in a single strike. My Dawn then activated Peony Blossom Attack, striking at the Lunar for the second time that turn. The Lunar attempted to react with Invincible Iron Bastion and a full excellency, but Parry 13 did not defend it from an attack with 21 successes. The Dawn did a total of 14 decisive damage, putting the Lunar just barely into its -4s in round one. However, my Lunar activated <i>The Tower Still Stands</i>, putting him back at 16 initiative. Both fighters are now unmounted, as the Solar lept off his mount to deliver that blow (SBRA allows you to do this).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So now that it's over I can share with you all that War Pig is an Essence 5 Lunar with all the charms for the Barbarian Warlord on page 546. He adds his wound penalties to his attacks, damage and soak. The Octavian Charms I gave him were <i>Crimson Spray Blur, Invincible Iron Bastion</i> and <i>Superior Strength Reversal</i>. I further added some custom charms that let him reflexively roll a disarm gambit before making a withering or decisive attack, with the gambit being unblockable; he can reflexively re-roll tens on his attack and damage rolls by spending one mote per re-roll; and he can spend health levels to power his physical excellencies, gaining (Wound Penalty) dice per level of damage he sacrifices.<br /> <br /> Here is what happened:<br /> <br /> On round two War Pig was ambushed by the party Night in tandem with her Owl-Griffon using <i>Deadly Onslaught Coordination</i> but his soak was so high that both rolled ping for just a handful of damage. The Dawn also suffered an ambush attack from the Trickster Lunar, but his soak was so high that she also rolled ping, doing no damage at all. Then my Dawn and I traded blows, I lead with a withering attack using that reflexive disarm gambit but he used <i>Heavenly Guardian Defense</i> to parry it <i>and </i>the withering attack despite a full excellency, willpower and major stunt for both rolls. He also counterattacked with <i>Flashing Edge of Dawn</i>, reducing War Pig to just two initiative and taking a chunk of his health. On his own turn my Dawn attacked and I attempted to counter with <i>Superior Strength Reversal</i> but I had no motes left and used my last two health levels and initiative to power the charm, hoping to at least do some withering damage. But instead my Dawn won the clash, having saved more motes than me, crashing War Pig even as he was passing out.<br /> <br /> I was more than a little put out by this outcome, so I asked my Dawn's player to redo the fight with me as a simulation starting from turn one. He somehow did even better than the first time. He lost his sword to the reflexive disarm but then took War Pig's lance with an improved disarm gambit (I set this at diff 4) and crashed him on turn two. The NPCs piled on the decisive damage since he had no hardness at that point, and War Pig never got to make a third attack.<br /> <br /> I spent four weeks designing War Pig. I often wondered if I was over-doing it, and I honestly don't think I could have made him any more difficult than he was. So does anyone see something that I'm missing? I'm at a loss here, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-19-2016, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T03:59:41-07:00","id":868308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=864688#post864688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which gives me a fun terrestrial charm concept I might battle-test soon:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Rising Elemental Fury</b></i><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental; Mins: ??? 1 Essence 1;<b> Prerequisites: </b>none; <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial exalt claims the tumult of battle as their own, and commences their onslaught with an eye for capitalizing on the chaos of a coordinated attack. This charm supplements a physical strike, and adds a number of non-charm bonus dice to the attack roll of a withering or decisive attack equal to the target's current Onslaught Penalty. If the target is suffering Onslaught Penalties from another Terrestrial exalt when this charm is invoked, then the user may claim these non-charm bonus dice even if their target is using a charm or effect that allows them to ignore Onslaught Penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you need the last addendum here that much as most charms which ignore onslaught penalties, i.e. fivefold bulwark stance, ignore them for the purposes of defence but they should still be around to take advantage off for charms like this anyway. This came up elsewhere in a discussion of furious jab I think.<br /> <br /> As for how to challenge your dawn, I think a dawn who has gone complete murder monster is genuinely very hard to challenge although you could just make a dusk caste I suppose, how did your dawn consistently get 20+ successes by the way as that seems high even for a full exellancy+other charms. I suspect you were also in the replay quite nice to let him steal, break the atunement of the lunar, attune himself and then ready the dire-lance in a single turn as this is something that a charm deep in the larceny tree (Iron Wolves grasp) is normally needed to do, although to be fair that charm does let you do it reflexively.<br /> <br /> One thing we've found in my game is that outnumbering counts for a lot, even people who are not particularly good in combat can help a lot as they add onslaught penalties and plink away at initiative and even get some significant decisive damage in if they are left alone as low priority targets this seems to have happened a bit here as the npc's you gave the dawn did a lot of damage, although they do tend to need to be battle groups,have high soak or have someone who can easily defend other them or they can just act as initiative batteries. I suspect for example that you would have more luck with two or three potent combatants than trying to stat up one mega creature. Also if your dawn has soak 20 some form of soak negation seems like a must. Otherwise he will never be crashed and with heavenly guardian defence there is little point in deceisives until he is.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11074-daltormind","name":"Daltormind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T11:28:06-07:00","id":868606,"title":"","content":"A few things jump out at me, reading that.<br /> <br /> First, the Lunar only has 11 dice to hit and Parry 6. Assuming the Dawn has Parry 7 and 14 dice to hit, which is easily possible at chargen (even for a mortal), when both attack with a one-point stunt the Dawn will land about 70% of their hits and the Lunar will land about 33%. This is an enormous advantage for the Dawn.<br /> <br /> Second, you had the Lunar charge past the Dawn in the first round. That sounds like something you'd do if you were deliberately trying to lose the fight.<br /> <br /> Third, the Dawn somehow has 20 soak. How'd he pull that off?<br /> <br /> Fourth, the Dawn somehow did 14 withering damage in one hit to an opponent with 20 soak. Again, how?<br /> <br /> Fifth, you apparently gave the Dawn a bunch of NPC allies. Again, that sounds like something you'd do if you were trying to lose<br /> <br /> Sixth, the Lunar was apparently knocked into his -4s while using The Tower Still Stands. But that Charm should've stopped the damage at his last -0 health level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T12:02:37-07:00","id":868637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the Lunar only has 11 dice to hit and Parry 6. Assuming the Dawn has Parry 7 and 14 dice to hit, which is easily possible at chargen (even for a mortal), when both attack with a one-point stunt the Dawn will land about 70% of their hits and the Lunar will land about 33%. This is an enormous advantage for the Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm understanding your math here. Eleven is War Pig's accuracy before charms, weapon accuracy or stunts, in other words his attribute, ability rating and specialty. My Dawn had the same base pool. Weapon choices account for the only major differences between them, as War Pig was using a heavy artifact weapon and my Dawn was using a medium mundane sword and shield, hence his better parry and accuracy. War Pig had by far the better damage and Piercing, but never landed a hit in either fight. And whereas War Pig lost the first round to stunting for the rest of the fight he was one step behind the Dawn for stunt level on attack and defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, you had the Lunar charge past the Dawn in the first round. That sounds like something you'd do if you were deliberately trying to lose the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't charge past the Dawn, his mount did and both riders fell to ground combat after round one. Round one was just a clash attack that War Pig lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, the Dawn somehow has 20 soak. How'd he pull that off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stamina five, soak eleven, and I let him add his Intimacy to his soak if applicable as an evocation. War Pig has equal soak because of his <i>Deadly Beastman Transformation</i>, and then four <i>better</i> soak when at his -4 health levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth, the Dawn somehow did 14 withering damage in one hit to an opponent with 20 soak. Again, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>My Dawn player would be better equipped to answer that since he somehow remembers all the numbers from every fight he is in, but after War Pig lost 3-5 initiative to the NPC allies (during the actual play) he rolled more or less unopposed (War Pig still suffers Wound Penalties to Defense) and did very well on the roll to hit with <i>Flashing Edge of Dawn</i>. Those withering damage dice then became decisive damage dice, thanks to how that charm works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth, you apparently gave the Dawn a bunch of NPC allies. Again, that sounds like something you'd do if you were trying to lose</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice I didn't expect it to help much since none of them were equipped to overcome War Pig's monstrous soak and could only roll ping damage. I expected that, if anything, War Pig could use them as initiative pinatas, but I forgot that with <i>War Lion Stance</i> an attack on an ally is just as difficult as an attack on the main target. Being able to starve your opponent for initiative is a very effective tactic, so in that way <i>WLS</i> is one of the best charms in the game. I did, admittedly, completely forget that the Night had her familiar to attack with as well, but I thought that the Night's contributions would be outweighed by the Lunar Trickster's damage, since War Pig relies very little on his Defense whereas my Dawn relies on it a lot so an ambush, I thought, would be quite effective. Wrong, apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sixth, the Lunar was apparently knocked into his -4s while using The Tower Still Stands. But that Charm should've stopped the damage at his last -0 health level.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;..., if a single attack would deal enough damage to completely fill all his health levels of one type and then spill over to the next, then all excess damage is prevented.&quot;<br /> <br /> I read this very differently, interpreting it to mean that if an attack would roll over <i>bashing</i> damage into <i>lethal,</i> the charm would stop that. Your interpretation makes sense, though War Pig does function much better at his -4 health level so really, that would have been a mixed blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T12:18:34-07:00","id":868654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read this very differently, interpreting it to mean that if an attack would roll over <i>bashing</i> damage into <i>lethal,</i> the charm would stop that. Your interpretation makes sense, though War Pig does function much better at his -4 health level so really, that would have been a mixed blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher stats on the edge of death is not necessarily better than a few extra rounds of combat gained by having extra life. And I agree with Sanctaphrax's reading of the charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T12:30:12-07:00","id":868666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'm understanding your math here. Eleven is War Pig's accuracy before charms, weapon accuracy or stunts, in other words his attribute, ability rating and specialty. My Dawn had the same base pool. Weapon choices account for the only major differences between them, as War Pig was using a heavy artifact weapon and my Dawn was using a medium mundane sword and shield, hence his better parry and accuracy. War Pig had by far the better damage and Piercing, but never landed a hit in either fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I thought &quot;11 dice to hit&quot; meant that when he rolls to hit, he rolls 11 dice.<br /> <br /> The +1 accuracy from the lance does make it a bit better. But I still think you'd have better luck with a light weapon and a shield.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And whereas War Pig lost the first round to stunting for the rest of the fight he was one step behind the Dawn for stunt level on attack and defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this happens often, it might be part of the reason your Dawn seems so unstoppable. +1 success to everything is a big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He didn't charge past the Dawn, his mount did and both riders fell to ground combat after round one. Round one was just a clash attack that War Pig lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make it less bad. Still dubious strategy, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stamina five, soak eleven, and I let him add his Intimacy to his soak if applicable as an evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it didn't affect this fight, but that sounds a bit unbalanced to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Dawn player would be better equipped to answer that since he somehow remembers all the numbers from every fight he is in, but after War Pig lost 3-5 initiative to the NPC allies (during the actual play) he rolled more or less unopposed (War Pig still suffers Wound Penalties to Defense) and did very well on the roll to hit with <i>Flashing Edge of Dawn</i>. Those withering damage dice then became decisive damage dice, thanks to how that charm works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about this bit: &quot;My Lunar gets 18 to hit on the clash but my Dawn rolls 20+, then does 14 withering damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's say the Dawn got 23 successes, so he hit by 5. Assume he has strength 5. With a mundane medium weapon, he's still doing ping damage. 9+5+5 = 19, which is less than the pig's soak. So how'd he get to 14 damage?<br /> <br /> He does get the automatic damage for winning the clash, but that's not 14 points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice I didn't expect it to help much since none of them were equipped to overcome War Pig's monstrous soak and could only roll ping damage. I expected that, if anything, War Pig could use them as initiative pinatas, but I forgot that with <i>War Lion Stance</i> an attack on an ally is just as difficult as an attack on the main target. Being able to starve your opponent for initiative is a very effective tactic, so in that way <i>WLS</i> is one of the best charms in the game. I did, admittedly, completely forget that the Night had her familiar to attack with as well, but I thought that the Night's contributions would be outweighed by the Lunar Trickster's damage, since War Pig relies very little on his Defense whereas my Dawn relies on it a lot so an ambush, I thought, would be quite effective. Wrong, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pig still takes Onslaught penalties, right? Those things are pretty brutal.<br /> <br /> How does the pig rely less on Defense than the Dawn? They have similar Parry and soak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868637#post868637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;..., if a single attack would deal enough damage to completely fill all his health levels of one type and then spill over to the next, then all excess damage is prevented.&quot;<br /> <br /> I read this very differently, interpreting it to mean that if an attack would roll over <i>bashing</i> damage into <i>lethal,</i> the charm would stop that. Your interpretation makes sense, though War Pig does function much better at his -4 health level so really, that would have been a mixed blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, he'll get to his -4s eventually. In the meantime, he could conserve his motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:07:39-07:00","id":868686,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that damage value makes absolutely no sense. Even with a grand daiklave and straight 10s on the damage roll you'd struggle to pull 14 damage out against someone with 20 soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:14:20-07:00","id":868692,"title":"","content":"As far as doing damage since it was a clash the lunar dv was 0 for the strike at 21 successes to hit the damage was 9+4+21=34 -20 was 14 damage which rolled very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:27:41-07:00","id":868706,"title":"","content":"Aside from the <i>TTSS </i>element (and I do agree that was a very costly error), it sounds like War Pig ran out of gas early too. That's a problem for someone whose entire kit sounds like it is built to win the long game. Octavian's Charms are costed for Octavian, after all, and he's got 40+ more motes over even an Essence 5 Lunar. Even if he hadn't run out of HLs, he was already spent. Also, it sounds like you went all-in by gambling on the early exchanges (which you lost). That seems like a bad move for a character whose advantages appear to favor the long fight rather than the short one.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the disappointing outcome is probably the result of some combination of gameplay errors (i.e. <i>TTSS</i>), strategic missteps, and some bad dice luck. After all, if you'd won those early exchanges things would have been different.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I hope that doesn't come across as overly critical. You asked for what you could've done differently and this is my best guess based on the available information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":1315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","user":"Ferryman","date":". 04-19-2016, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:29:12-07:00","id":868708,"title":"","content":"In a Clash, the attack roll essentially counts as a defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clash Attacks ignore both characters\u2019 Defense. Instead, <br /> the two attacks act as an opposed roll (p. 189). The character who accumulates more successes wins, striking<br /> his opponent, while the loser\u2019s attack is thwarted. <b>If a <br /> Clash Attack is withering, then it adds the threshold by <br /> which the winning fighter beat his opponent\u2019s roll to its <br /> raw damage.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:30:23-07:00","id":868710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868273#post868273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dawn also suffered an ambush attack from the Trickster Lunar, but his soak was so high that she also rolled ping, doing no damage at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad luck and all, but against an armored guy like that, a crafty trickster allied to a powerhouse warrior might have been better served by a surprise Distract or Disarm gambit instead, no?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then my Dawn and I traded blows, I lead with a withering attack using that reflexive disarm gambit but he used <i>Heavenly Guardian Defense</i> to parry it <i>and </i>the withering attack despite a full excellency, willpower and major stunt for both rolls. </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading it right, you mean he used HGD to parry both the reflexive Gambit <b>and </b>the Withering Attack? If so, <b>how</b>? HGD doesn't work against Withering attacks.<br /> <br /> Also, an opponent who doesn't do much for Defenses, even if remarkable at tanking attacks, against a Dawn with also great tanking ability <i>and </i>superior defenses <i>and </i>a bunch of buddies/pets? That smells like a losing proposition from the start (also, yeah, forgetting about War Lion Stance when hoping to use the the dude's allies as easier Initiative sources was a big mistake).<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know if this is the case, but if the Lunars knew they were up against Solars or at least powerful Exalts or something of that scale and depending on their personality (but seems appropriate for a trickster, at least), maybe they might have made more use of their Lunarness in their favor? Examples:<br /> <br /> Nearly killed by a swordsman? Grow wings and start pelting them with thrown weapons from afar.<br /> <br /> Doing an ambush? Attack when it is misty/dark or throw smoke bombs or something, then make use of animal senses and Perception Charms to have most enemies at a disadvantage. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(well, &quot;attack when they are asleep&quot; would be even better, but only if you made sure that the players are aware of such considerations will be part of the game, so they might at least have a rotation of sentries or something to give a decent chance of catching the attack. Or at least just murder a couple of the NPCs and have their screams wake up the party. Maybe have a minion attack the Night if he needs a chance to show off his Awareness Charms)</span><br /> <br /> If you have time, enter their camp as a small animal, poison their supplies, then attack after they are not well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T13:33:35-07:00","id":868711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868708#post868708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Clash, the attack roll essentially counts as a defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Pig would have had to roll 0 successes on his attack for Korekore's math to work in a clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:22:18-07:00","id":868762,"title":"","content":"I did as my gm advised without reading myself and it worked out for me in this circumstance. I haven't gotten to do a full read of the book yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:24:25-07:00","id":868765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868762#post868762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did as my gm advised without reading myself and it worked out for me in this circumstance. I haven't gotten to do a full read of the book yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's attacking you. All is cool. We're just trying to help the GM who was trying to figure out how to make a challenge. What they had would have stood a better chance with the proper rules. Mistakes happen, we all make them (especially with a new edition) and it'll be better next time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:32:47-07:00","id":868773,"title":"","content":"Well he is taking a break and I am going to be running the game in his stead. So I will probably be the one asking for help here in a few weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:38:21-07:00","id":868780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868773#post868773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well he is taking a break and I am going to be running the game in his stead. So I will probably be the one asking for help here in a few weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what we're here for! And this thread has a lot of great advice already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:14:22-07:00","id":868868,"title":"","content":"Actually I've decided to permanently hand over the reins to Korekore for this story. I hope he will continue to keep you all appraised with his observations, you have been tremendously helpful and i think he will prove he has very useful observations once he has had a chance to read through all the rules.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd like to thank everyone for all the advice you've given me. I think this just isn't a good system for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-19-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T18:50:40-07:00","id":868979,"title":"","content":"So my major take aways based on what I have heard from people here about this fight:<br /> <br /> 1. I just flat-out got the rules wrong about clashes, disarming artifacts and <i>TTSS</i>, and the fight would have been very different if I had used the rules correctly. In my defense, Exalted has always been a system that requires STs to memorize a tremendous amount of rules and information, and maybe that makes it a bad fit for me.<br /> <br /> 2. I shouldn't have given my Dawn something that would permanently increase his soak up to 20. As a side note I also ruled that his armor was environmentally sealed and I can't tell you what a mistake that has been. I could have been dousing him with environmental effects like poison and drowning this whole time if not for that. Lunars get these kind of soak numbers, a Solar with these plus their insane Defense ratings is just too much.<br /> <br /> 3. <i>War Lion Stance </i>is probably the best melee charm. Seriously, if your Dawn is already impossible to hit, and they have <i>Bulwark Stance </i>on, then allowing every ally within short range that same protection just starves out the antagonists while also adding extra attacks each round that at least do ping damage with no real drawback.<br /> <br /> 4. I paired the wrong personality to this charmset. War Pig is a big and rowdy berserker type that uses a full physical excellency when he attacks because that makes the fight fun for him. If I had built the exact some Lunar as a turtle totem or something I would probably have just sat back each round using <i>Impenetrable Beastman Hide</i> until my Dawn mote tapped himself, and I would have won.<br /> <br /> 5. Gambits are better than 1-2 ping damage. I could have easily disarmed my Dawn on round two with that Trickster since we ruled that she had ambush. I could have also distracted him, or gotten him in grapple which would have been a real bad time for him. But instead I was focused on crashing him because he had had an initiative reset, and the result was extremely underwhelming.<br /> <br /> So apparently the consensus is that if I don't switch to being a player in this Ex3 game then there won't be enough people to justify continuing it, but I'm pretty well and truly done with this system. Everyone here was a real help, and I wouldn't have gotten half as much done without your ideas and support. I hope this thread has been of some use, and maybe it'll continue to be helpful to you in your games. I certainly hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-20-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:16:42-07:00","id":869047,"title":"","content":"Huh.<br /> <br /> I don't know why but I feel kinda sad about that. <br /> <br /> If the sheer crunch and complexity of EX3 is driving you away, despite your obvious willingness to put in time, that's not a good sign for the game's future.<br /> <br /> Well, good luck with whatever you play next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:36:13-07:00","id":869058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>War Lion Stance </i>is probably the best melee charm. </div> </div> </div>War Lion Stance is amazing. It's essentially saved the Changing Moon in my game twice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T03:25:12-07:00","id":870064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle#post835958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finding that it can be very difficult to challenge the might of a full circle of Solar exalts, so I'm making this thread for STs to share their ideas and experiences. Feel free to post non-combat challenges as well, anything to break up the often boring steam-roller sensation of besting obstacle after obstacle without even busting out a full excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance we can get a copy of your Dawn's build? Have seen it referenced a few times, but don't know full numbers etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=869058#post869058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Lion Stance is amazing. It's essentially saved the Changing Moon in my game twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if it has been said elsewhere, but it is worth noting it only works on one ally at a time, not the entire party!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","user":"Molez","date":". 04-21-2016, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:23:42-07:00","id":870102,"title":"","content":"Sure, but as it's reflexive, unless two people are being attacked simultaneously, you can just drop it, activate it to defend someone else, then go back again. It's only 2m after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:58:29-07:00","id":870117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=870102#post870102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but as it's reflexive, unless two people are being attacked simultaneously, you can just drop it, activate it to defend someone else, then go back again. It's only 2m after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That becomes a pretty quick way to get mote tapped, also I don't think it would do anything to help against a battlegroup attack, as they are all made at once, so you could be defending only one other at that point in time... battlegroups with a good command action are a threat/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:08:26-07:00","id":870123,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I was thinking of when I said it wouldn't work if two people were being attack simultaneously, as battle groups do that.<br /> <br /> But the Eclipse just guards the Changing Moon, who's the only one who both fights and and isn't that tough (the others are either tough or try not to fight).<br /> <br /> It is kind of weird the way the Eclipse often takes the same attack twice, since the BG's attack is applied against everyone, but the Eclipse takes the Changing Moon's attack against herself as well. But I guess since it represents several soldiers attacking, it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:22:56-07:00","id":870132,"title":"","content":"My players challenge themselves fairly regularly, making things harder on themselves then digging back out, but as has been posted else where, outnumbering them in combat is big. And I have found that means outnumbering with actual actors, not (only) battlegroups. They can indeed be formidible, but if you're still left at a 4 on 6 fight (yeah I have six players) they're gonna chew through the opposition, especially if they're not shy about anima flare. Of course like I said, this can make life harder on them in the long run, the Zenith just ran himself all alone into an ambush by a competent team of Anathema hunters (two DBs and three mortal archers, my version of the impromptu level of a Wyld Hunt) He's got solid resistance, his Presence Supernal let him sap a ton of Willpower from his attackers, and he ate an attack that would have killed just about any other character twice over, but now he's badly wounded, poisoned and still outnumbers 2 to 5. Next session is gonna be a nail biter (Yeah we had to end there. Cliffhanger!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1398-corwin859","name":"corwin859","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:30:07-07:00","id":870181,"title":"","content":"While I haven't tried it, I'd worry that (as I have 6 players) outnumbering them would be far too many characters to handle, and be too long. I'd rather just throw 2 hard npcs and a buff battle group at them. I'd like giving them hard battles... but it's more important to give them battles that don't drag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:29:52-07:00","id":870323,"title":"","content":"I completely agree, which is why this is the first time I've really done it, and it was almost by accident. The other thing to help create that dynamic would to have something else also going on, a messenger escaping, an orphanage burning down, something that needs to be handled WHILE the fight happens, that way not everyone can focus on the fight (at least if they want to save the burning orphans.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1398-corwin859","name":"corwin859","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:30:26-07:00","id":870380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=868606#post868606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things jump out at me, reading that.<br /> Sixth, the Lunar was apparently knocked into his -4s while using The Tower Still Stands. But that Charm should've stopped the damage at his last -0 health level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just caught this. Looking at the power in the book I have to say, I agree with kindledRadial's read. -4, -2, 0's, etc. are not types of damage, they are markers for effects based on amount of damage taken. Lethal, bashing, and aggravated are types of damage, at least I think so, unless I am missing something. Is there somewhere else in the book that says the wound penalties are rollover areas and types of damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:41:34-07:00","id":870394,"title":"","content":"I think the part you're missing is that if the Charm worked that way, it would only kick in when Octavian had just been defeated. Since the devs ran a mock combat between Ahlat and Octavian in which the latter used this Charm and <i>didn't</i> immediately fall unconscious, I think it's pretty clear that's not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:22:03-07:00","id":870447,"title":"","content":"It says &quot;all his health levels of one type&quot;, which I took to mean wound penalty. But to tell the truth, my opinion is based entirely on the assumption that the Charm is supposed to be useful. If one reading is powerful and the other sucks, I'm going to assume the powerful one is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:23:53-07:00","id":870451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=870447#post870447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says &quot;all his health levels of one type&quot;, which I took to mean wound penalty. But to tell the truth, my opinion is based entirely on the assumption that the Charm is supposed to be useful. If one reading is powerful and the other sucks, I'm going to assume the powerful one is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my reading as well, and I'm confident it's the correct one. John tweeted a battle between Octavian and Ahlat in which Octavian used it, and as I recall that was how it worked then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T21:28:19-07:00","id":870915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=870117#post870117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That becomes a pretty quick way to get mote tapped, also I don't think it would do anything to help against a battlegroup attack, as they are all made at once, so you could be defending only one other at that point in time... battlegroups with a good command action are a threat/</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first ran into this situation I ruled that my Dawn could use one instance of <i>War Lion Stance</i> to defend his circle, and I immediately regretted it. What I ruled afterwards was that he had to activate WLS for every subject he wants to defend, and he could only defend multiple subjects from area effects (like battlegroup damage) if he used WLS and <i>Heavenly Guardian Defense</i> for <i>each</i> person he wanted to defend, or 6m per ally per area attack. I'm sure this wasn't something they intended to allow in the write-up for HGD, but I like giving my Dawn the option to mote-tap himself in one turn. Never came up though.<br /> <br /> And as far as <i>The Tower Still Stands</i> is concerned, I'm pretty sure that my initial interpretation was wrong. If that charm worked as I had imagined, then Octavian would gain initiative even after having his health filled with bashing. But he doesn't have any charms or abilities that keep him up when he is full of bashing, so basically the initiative gains would at that point be pointless. I wish it had been worded more clearly, but the only useful interpretation is that he can use that charm to prevent damage from aggravating his wound penalties, though I should note that as written it's also ambiguous to me whether or not he can use that charm <i>again</i> once all his health levels of one penalty are filled. Clarification would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-22-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T23:22:32-07:00","id":870984,"title":"","content":"tl;dr: give your big bads a martial art style and a couple of charms meant to compliment its strengths. Soak SERIOUSLY prolongs a fight and increases the viability of social influence in combat. It is really good. Battle groups are also great, and sprinkling the opposition with lieutenants giving Command bonuses gives only mildly fighty characters some high priority targets to focus on.<br /> <br /> Hey <b>Northgame</b> people, <b>don't read this</b>. Spoilers! Sort of!<br /> <br /> I had great fun playing an obnoxious (and damaged) elder Changing Moon against my Circle of Essence 1 Solars in a scene that was half combat and half social influence. She's playing the role of a secondary but potent adversary right now. They caught her in the act of sabotaging their followers and vessel, but she managed to temporarily incapacitate a few mortal lieutenants before they rolled Join Battle. That is surprisingly important, because War God Descendent is a hell of a trick, and you do not want even mediocre battle groups rolling attacks against you with even mediocre leadership backing them up.<br /> <br /> They played 'nice' for three rounds before talking her down, and she completely depleted the Dawn's essence pool and a great deal of their willpower with the following tricks:<br /> <br /> Full Mastery of Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style.<br /> Bitter Medicine Bait: When someone spends a willpower to ignore her Inspire attempt, she may spend 4 motes and 1 willpower to immediately Instill a Minor Tie of Guilt towards her, without needing to roll. This effect applies to everyone affected by the original Inspire attempt who chooses to resist. Willpower paid to ignore this automatic Instill effect is awarded to the Lunar. 1/scene per target.<br /> Hide Like Tusks: +8 soak until her next turn for 4m1w. 1/scene, reset when she resists a withering attack of at least 15 raw damage without suffering initiative loss.<br /> Hidden Mirror Smile: When her Solar mate (the Dawn) rolls in opposition to her for any effect, she may spend a mote to roll all of her mate's 1s as dice on her own behalf. This effect may not be used if her mate says her name while executing the action, and every time this charm is successfully used, the Solar mate is entitled to a Wits+Integrity check (difficulty 5) to remember this name, even if she's never heard it before. If the party ever figures out the trick to this, I expect &quot;TETSUUUOOO!&quot; style shouts with every stunt.<br /> <br /> High combat pools, influence pools, and guile, with matching Lunar Excellencies. No sorcery, lore, medicine, or other support tricks.<br /> With her high Essence Lunar hax, Fragrant Petal Fascination Kata, Seven Storms Escape Prana, and Demure Carp Feint, she was exceedingly difficult to pin down, much less kill, even for a very combat-heavy Circle. They ended up convincing her to leave, but she gave the Zenith a 10 HL kick to the face with Pillow Book on her way out. (It's cool; he's supernal resistance, and it's his own fault for Fluttering Cry of Warning! every damn attack.)<br /> <br /> In reserve, she also had:<br /> Predator Grace Method<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> Full Mastery of White Reaper Style<br /> Moon Healing Escalation: When assuming Deadly Beastman Transformation, she recovers half of her spent motes and half of her wounded health levels.<br /> <br /> Playing rough was not necessary. IIRC, she used Revolving Crescent Defense once.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether Lunars can actually attain use of the Mastery keyword for martial arts styles, but DPC and WRS seemed like good approximations for Changing Moon and Full Moon style ass-kicking. After reading the charms and figuring out how the fighting style worked for DPC, I asked myself what sort of native charms would make it absolutely infuriating to play against (along the lines of Solar Socialize and Black Claw Style's synergy), and invented some probably-too-cheap-to-be-balanced supplements for it. It was an entertaining encounter, and the willpower-stealing drama bomb that was Bitter Medicine Bait was most satisfying.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Previous opponents that got a satisfactory stunt out of every player include literally a hundred first circle demons split into three battle groups with competent leadership, under the overall command of a Terrestrial Ebon Shadow Stylist. Against four Solars and two Battle Groups aboard the Supernal Sailor's personal vessel, this was a hell of a fight. Naval Maneuvering and an Ambush reversal by the Dawn turned it into a surprisingly quick encounter, but enough of the Circle's followers were killed in the melee to make for some interesting character moments afterwards. The Zenith got his caste Solar XP by starting a tradition of raiding the captain's personal store of liquor to honor the dead.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Since the Circle is relatively combat heavy (and to establish the depth of their supernatural opposition--House Ledaal wants their Twilight dead, and the Lunar wants to bleed the Dawn slowly for her role in her own previous incarnation's demise) the first four sessions have featured some big fights. I'm looking forward to pivoting into a more political environment for the next few sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:10:08-07:00","id":871173,"title":"","content":"This may be too little, too late sort of advice, and may have already been covered, but I didn't see it in my somewhat hasty read-through of the thread. Apologies if I missed it.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the best way to re-introduce challenge to a party that is mighty in combat is not to scale up the combat, but to change the stakes. Don't make it about life-or-death for the party. Make it about the goals the party is pursuing, and the goals the opponents are pursuing. The combat-focused Dawn will probably slaughter whatever he puts his daiklaive to, to whatever degree of slaughter he chooses. Let him. Challenge him not with something that can &quot;take it&quot; or that can &quot;dish it out&quot; to him, but with the need to prioritize what he kills, or to be cautious with his kill-choices. With the time taken to beat something providing crucial delays before he can get to the victory condition for the party, or prevent the enemy from achieving theirs.<br /> <br /> As an example that doesn't QUITE fit here, but hopefully illustrates the notion, consider a classic: the party is serving as escorts for a trade caravan, and it comes under assault by bandits. The bandits' goal is not murder (though they're not above it); it's getting as much loot as they can and getting away with it. The party's goal is not mere survival, nor the slaughter of the bandits (though the latter would achieve their goal); it's preventing damage and theft of life and property.<br /> <br /> The challenge is not even binary, here; each time the bandits damage something or kill an NPC, it's a mark against the party. Each thing the bandits get to run away with is a mark in their favor. Driving the bandits off before they do any permanent damage is total victory as much as slaughtering the bandits outright before they can do any permanent damage. Having the bandits come in, kill a few NPCs, and ride off with 10-30% of the goods is a pretty hefty loss, even if the PCs never take more than withering damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:10:53-07:00","id":871494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=871173#post871173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, the best way to re-introduce challenge to a party that is mighty in combat is not to scale up the combat, but to change the stakes. Don't make it about life-or-death for the party. Make it about the goals the party is pursuing, and the goals the opponents are pursuing. The combat-focused Dawn will probably slaughter whatever he puts his daiklaive to, to whatever degree of slaughter he chooses. Let him. Challenge him not with something that can &quot;take it&quot; or that can &quot;dish it out&quot; to him, but with the need to prioritize what he kills, or to be cautious with his kill-choices. With the time taken to beat something providing crucial delays before he can get to the victory condition for the party, or prevent the enemy from achieving theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for posting Segev! What you are proposing does indeed work, and I would say is probably the <i>best </i>available option for STs (like myself) who find it difficult to impossible to out-play their players. I'm also a big fan of the moral quandary story: maybe in your example the party decides to chase some of those bandits down and take the stolen loot back, but they find that the bandits are just trying to feed their families after losing their livlihoods after the Guild moved in, or worse, they're all former Guild slaves. Now perhaps you have a story where you have to make things right and help mere mortals fend for themselves in the second age, without your constant assistance. That's a very Solar-appropriate story.<br /> <br /> What I will say though is that it's frustrating that these narratives are <i>necessary</i>, because the system doesn't readily support challenging stand-up brawls past an early point. At least it didn't for me at my table, after considerable efforts to bump up the antagonist difficulty. It's very important to remember that the story itself can present challenges that aren't resolved with simple opposed rolls, but I still wish that a mechanical challenge was more feasible in this system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:36:26-07:00","id":871609,"title":"","content":"I'm glad it's helpful to some. I will say that I actually think this kind of encounter design leads to better games, overall, for many of the reasons you noted, kindledRadial. I think too often GMs get into a habit of viewing combat as a &quot;kill or be killed&quot; thing, &quot;to the death,&quot; and that leads to a trap wherein one might accidentally start equating &quot;having a fight to the death&quot; with &quot;a challenge.&quot; Really, that isn't the challenge, even if it is the source of difficulty and risk. The challenge should always be something with greater stakes to the player than merely &quot;will my character survive?&quot;<br /> <br /> I know, life-or-death is one of the greatest true risks out there, but because this is a game, we often trivialize it. It also means, with stakes at the &quot;do or die&quot; level, that the PCs <u>must</u> always win. If they don't, they die, and that means that the game is over, if only for that character. You can have victory become a more meaningfully uncertain quality of a conflict if there is something at stake that, even if lost, does not stop the PCs from being able to continue participating in the game's ongoing events.<br /> <br /> So honestly, while I voice this advice for GMs whose parties are hard to challenge in combat (often due to one combat monster overshadowing the other PCs, making it either &quot;challenge him&quot; or &quot;kill everybody else&quot;), it's advice I think is good in general.<br /> <br /> If you really need the &quot;fight is challenging just because the stats are that grueling&quot; thing...save it for when you've got a chance to do one-on-ones or other things that will allow you to separate the PCs into groups that fight at more even levels, and pit them against challenges for them. It will likely be rare, so you can do it this way without always splitting up the party every time conflict breaks out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:46:04-07:00","id":872561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/835958-ex3-how-to-challenge-a-full-solar-circle?p=870064#post870064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any chance we can get a copy of your Dawn's build? Have seen it referenced a few times, but don't know full numbers etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Name: Captain Yuri Kochiyama of the Solar deliberative 17th Gunzosha Field Force</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Caste: Dawn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Limit trigger Being forced to lie or break a oath</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Limit break chains of honor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Defining: Everyone deserves life freedom and happiness as long as it does not infringe on the rights of another +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Defining: Sol has appointed me to make the world better +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: In every war there are innocents needing protection +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Oppression is the greatest evil -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Children are precious +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Cast +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: The circle +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Enemies of Creation -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Haki +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Family is important +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Major: Truth +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor: Veronica +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor Umi +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor Doll +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor: One must never stop learning +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor: indomitable Spirit +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Minor Apple Pie +</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Xp </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">SXP </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">STR 4 CHA 5 PER 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">DEX 5 MAN 1 INT 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">STA 5 APP 3 WITS 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Parry 6-8 (max gained from mounted benefit and overcome by reach weapons)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Evasion 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px